window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS=(window.MONARCH_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":276,"title":"Chapter 276: In Two Days","paragraphs":["\"Not bad. Another thousand mana points and around a hundred points in each of my physical stats, and I should be able to break through to the High stage of the Condensed Core. The mana being richer here and so many monster cores I got... I reached very fast to this level.\"","Noah gave a satisfied nod before closing the status window floating before his eyes.","\"Hah... this is nice.\"","After six months of relentless training, seeing his progress laid out before him always gave him a sense of accomplishment.","With a thought, the sword in his hand disappeared into his storage ring. Noah stretched his shoulders before turning toward the wooden house.","He had trained enough for now. As he stepped onto the veranda, a familiar voice reached him.","\"Decided to take a break?\"","\"Yeah.\"","Noah glanced toward the source of the voice and smiled.","\"I missed you, after all.\"","\"Shut up.\"","Akari’s response came almost immediately.","She was sitting gracefully on the wooden floor beside the open sliding door, quietly watching the yard where Noah had been training.","Noah chuckled and walked over before sitting beside her. \"You look cute each time I talk like that.\"","\"Oh... dear, you are delusional.\" She replied with small smile.","For a few moments, neither of them spoke. The gentle breeze passed through the open doorway, carrying the fresh scent of the surrounding forest with it.","Noah eventually broke the silence.","\"I’ve nearly mastered it.\"","\"The Aura?\"","\"Yeah.\"","Akari nodded.","\"I’ve been watching. Your control has improved considerably.\"","She glanced at him.","\"As your Core Rank increases, your control over mana will naturally improve as well. Your mana will become denser, and maintaining Aura should become much easier.\"","\"That’s what I’m hoping for.\"","Noah leaned back slightly, resting his hands against the wooden floor.","Then he remembered something.","\"What about you?\"","Akari turned toward him.","\"Hm?\"","\"Your training.\"","Noah’s expression became slightly more serious.","\"How is it going?\"","He paused before asking the question that had been on his mind for some time.","\"Do you think you’re finally ready?\"","Akari didn’t answer immediately.","Her blue, vertically slit eyes shifted toward the peaceful forest outside.","\"...Yes.\"","Her voice was calm.","\"I think I’m ready.\"","Noah watched her carefully.","Akari raised one hand and gently touched the dark sapphire scales covering the side of her neck.","\"I’ve been suppressing my bloodline for far too long.\"","Her fingers slowly traced the hardened scales.","\"I think it’s finally time to stop holding it back.\"","Noah remained silent. Over the past six months, Akari had told him considerably more about her dragon bloodline.","She was already capable of awakening it completely. That had never been the true problem. The problem was what happened after the awakening.","Akari had attempted it before.","More than once.","Whenever she allowed the dragon bloodline to awaken beyond a certain point, its power became increasingly difficult to control.","Her instincts changed. Her emotions became violent. Her thoughts grew clouded.","Eventually, the overwhelming instincts of the dragon began drowning out her rational mind.","Each time, Akari had been forced to suppress the awakening before she completely lost control of herself.","That was also why she had spent decades strengthening herself.","Training and meditating. Improving her control.","Strengthening both her body and mind.","And now, after reaching the very peak of the Sovereign Core’s High stage—the pinnacle of what was commonly considered the human ranks—Akari believed she was finally strong enough to withstand the complete awakening.","Noah looked at her seriously.","\"So you’re going to fully release it this time?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"And you won’t suppress it halfway through?\"","Akari slowly shook her head.","\"No.\"","Her expression hardened with determination.","\"This time, I’ll see it through until the end.\"","Noah stared at her for several seconds.","\"And if you lose control again?\"","Akari’s eyes shifted toward him.","There was no fear in them.","Only calm determination.","\"Then I’ll regain control.\"","A faint smile appeared on her lips.","\"I’ve spent sixty years preparing for this, Noah.\"","Her hand lowered from the scales on her neck.","\"If I’m still too afraid to take the final step after all that time...\"","She looked toward the endless forest.","\"...then all those years of training would have been meaningless.\"","Noah couldn’t argue with that.","He slowly nodded.","\"Alright.\"","His expression became serious.","\"Then when you do it, I’ll stay nearby.\"","Akari raised an eyebrow.","\"Noah—\"","\"Not close enough to interfere.\"","He quickly added before she could object.","\"But I’m not leaving you completely alone.\"","Akari stared at him for a moment.","Then her expression softened.","\"...Very well.\"","Noah smiled.","\"Good.\"","Akari turned her gaze back toward the forest.","Soon, she would stop suppressing the power she had restrained for decades.","And this time she intended to awaken the blood of the Storm Dragon completely.","\"By the way...\"","Noah suddenly remembered something.","\"According to the dragon who trapped you here, you’re supposed to be freed after fully awakening your bloodline, right?\"","Akari turned her gaze toward him.","\"Yes.\"","\"But you’ve already awakened it completely before, haven’t you? Even if you couldn’t control it, you still managed to fully awaken your bloodline for a few minutes.\"","Akari fell silent.","Noah continued thoughtfully.","\"So why are you still trapped here?\"","\"You’re not wrong.\"","Akari looked toward the distant forest.","\"I’ve wondered about that countless times over the years.\"","She gently touched the sapphire scales covering her neck.","\"But I don’t think simply awakening the bloodline is what he meant.\"","Noah raised an eyebrow.","\"What do you mean?\"","\"I believe complete awakening having full control and being in right state of mind.\"","Akari’s expression became thoughtful.","\"Or perhaps once I successfully awaken my bloodline and gain complete control over its power, I’ll acquire something I currently don’t possess.\"","\"Something like an ability?\"","\"Perhaps.\"","Akari nodded.","\"An instinct, inherited knowledge, a new ability... I don’t know.\"","She paused.","\"But if that happens, I may be able to find the exit myself.\"","Noah rubbed his chin.","\"That’s definitely possible.\"","Considering everything he had experienced inside the labyrinth, Noah wouldn’t be surprised if the method of escaping this place had been hidden within Akari herself all along.","He turned toward her.","\"Then when do we start?\"","Akari didn’t answer immediately.","Her blue, slit-pupiled eyes remained fixed on Noah for several seconds.","Despite her confidence earlier, Noah could see the faint hesitation buried beneath her calm expression.","This wasn’t merely another training session. She had attempted this before.","And she knew exactly what losing control felt like.","Finally, Akari exhaled softly.","\"...Two days from now.\"","\"Two days?\"","\"Yes.\"","She lowered her gaze toward her hands. Her fingers slowly curled.","\"I want some time to prepare myself mentally. To meditate, stabilize my mana, and make sure my mind is completely calm before I attempt the awakening.\"","Noah nodded in understanding.","\"Alright.\"","He gave her a small smile.","\"Two days from now, then.\"","Akari looked at him before returning the smile.","\"Yes.\"","Her gaze shifted toward the peaceful forest beyond the veranda.","\"In two days...\"","Her sapphire eyes narrowed with determination.","\"I’ll finally stop suppressing it.\""]},{"number":277,"title":"Chapter 277: Because I want to spoil you too","paragraphs":["Noah stretched both arms high above his head.","\"Two days... Sigh...\"","Then, without warning, he casually let his body fall sideways.","His head landed perfectly on Akari’s lap, resting comfortably against her thighs as though it were the most natural place in the world.","Akari raised an eyebrow.","\"...\"","But she didn’t complain.","After six months of living together, she had long since grown accustomed to Noah doing things like this. In fact, giving him a lap pillow after training had somehow become one of the most ordinary parts of their daily life.","Her hand naturally moved toward his snow-white hair.","She gently ran her fingers through it.","\"You are being spoiled again.\"","Noah closed his eyes comfortably.","\"What do you mean, spoiled? I just want to feel your affection.\"","Akari’s lips curved into a faint smile.","\"Doesn’t that mean you’re being spoiled?\"","\"I don’t know.\"","Noah opened one eye and looked up at her.","\"Why don’t you try it yourself?\"","Akari’s hand stopped.","\"Me?\"","She tilted her head.","\"What do you mean?\"","\"I mean...\"","Noah smiled mischievously.","\"Do you want to rest your head on my lap for once? Maybe let me hold you and spoil you instead.\"","\"...!\"","Akari’s cheeks immediately gained a faint pink hue.","For just a moment, she actually imagined herself resting comfortably against him while Noah stroked her hair. The thought alone made her strangely embarrassed. Her fingers immediately moved toward his cheek.","Pinch!","\"Ouch!\"","\"Here we go again.\"","She gently pulled his cheek.","\"You’ve started talking nonsense.\"","Noah caught her hand and freed his poor cheek.","\"It’s not nonsense!\"","He abruptly sat upright.","\"Then let’s try it.\"","Akari stared at him.","\"No.\"","\"Why not?\"","\"Because there is absolutely no need.\"","\"There is!\" Noah was in no mood to refuse.","\"Noah.\" She looked at him sternly.","\"You always let me rest on your lap. That’s unfair.\" Noah said with dejected expression.","\"How is that unfair?\"","\"Because I want to spoil you too.\"","Akari blinked. The sincerity with which he said those ridiculous words momentarily left her speechless. She shook her head.","\"There is no need for that.\"","How could she, a woman over ninety years old could let a young man spoil her like a kid. This was just not possible. Absolutely not.","But Noah was not someone who knows how to give up easily. \"You must!\" He insist.","Before Akari could protest again, Noah took her hand and gently pulled her toward him.","\"Noah—\"","Akari sighed helplessly. She could easily resist him if she genuinely wanted to. They both knew that. Yet instead of doing so, she reluctantly allowed herself to be guided downward.","Eventually, Akari found herself lying on the wooden floor of the veranda.","Her head rested across Noah’s lap.","\"...\"","\"...\"","An awkward silence followed.","Akari stared straight ahead.","Her cheeks slowly became warmer.","Noah’s thighs weren’t anything like hers. Months of physical training had made his legs muscular and firm, so they certainly weren’t the softest pillow in existence.","Yet strangely that wasn’t what made her heart beat faster. It was the situation itself. For months, she had been the one allowing Noah to rest against her.","She had stroked his hair. And she had comforted him. Spoiled him whenever he became exhausted from training. Now their positions had completely reversed.","’This is... surprisingly embarrassing.’","Akari tried maintaining her usual composed expression. Then she felt something warm settle gently against her head.","Noah’s hand.","His fingers slowly moved through her raven-black hair, careful not to disturb the elegant bun she had tied earlier.","Stroke.","Stroke.","Akari’s blue eyes widened slightly.","Noah looked down at her with a satisfied smile.","\"See?\"","His movements remained surprisingly gentle.","\"It’s not bad, right?\"","Akari remained silent for several seconds. Then her eyes slowly drifted closed.","\"It’s acceptable I guess.\"","Noah’s eyebrow twitched.","\"Just acceptable?\"","\"Don’t become arrogant.\"","\"Haha!\"","Noah continued stroking her hair.","For once, Akari didn’t have to be the master. Right now she didn’t have to train him, protect him, cook for him, or comfort him.","She could simply lie there and allow someone else to care for her. Despite embarrassing situation it felt strangely pleasant.","Akari relaxed a little more against his lap.","Noah noticed it immediately. His smile softened.","\"Looks like someone enjoys being spoiled too.\"","Akari opened one eye.","\"Noah.\"","\"Yes?\"","\"Be quiet and keep stroking my hair.\"","\"...\"","A huge grin spread across his face.","\"Yes, ma’am.\"","Akari closed her eyes again.","And this time, she didn’t bother hiding the small smile forming on her lips.","Noah noticed it and smile more widely. He leaned and gently kiss on her cheek. Her cheeks warm up as pink shade spread over her fair skin.","It was not his first time kissing her on cheek, for last many month he had kiss her too many times that she lost count.","But even after so many times she was not used to it, each time he land a gently kiss, heat would rose to her cheeks. Which gave her soft shade of pink.","They remained like that without talking to each other.","---","\"Hey, what are you cooking?\"","Noah’s voice suddenly came from behind her.","Before Akari could turn around, he stepped closer and casually rested his chin on her right shoulder, peering curiously at what she was preparing in the small wooden kitchen.","\"Nothing special,\" Akari replied, continuing her work. \"I’m just roasting some meat and making a spicy soup to go with it.\"","A few loose strands of her raven-black hair repeatedly fell across her face while she worked.","Noticing them, Noah raised his hand.","His fingers gently caught the strands and tucked them behind her ear.","Akari paused for a moment before continuing to prepare the food.","\"Thank you, Noah.\"","\"Hehe~ You’re welcome.\"","Noah remained where he was, watching her cook from over her shoulder.","The sight brought a strange smile to his face.","\"You know...\"","\"Hm?\"","\"It really feels like you’re my wife.\"","Bang!","The dagger Akari had been using as a kitchen knife struck the wooden cutting board much harder than necessary.","Her movements froze."]},{"number":278,"title":"Chapter 278: Cuddling","paragraphs":["Slowly, she turned her head toward him.","Because Noah’s chin was still resting on her shoulder, their faces were suddenly only inches apart.","Akari’s cheeks gained a faint pink hue.","\"T-That was a very bad joke.\"","Noah’s smile only widened.","\"Was it?\"","Before she could respond, his arms casually slipped around her waist from behind, settling over the obi wrapped around her kimono.","Akari stiffened.","\"No-Noah...\"","\"Hm?\"","\"I’m cooking.\"","She sounded embarrassed, but she made no genuine attempt to push him away.","Noah gently rubbed his cheek against her shoulder.","\"I know. Sorry for bothering you.\"","His arms remained around her for another moment.","\"I’m just bored sitting alone over there.\"","Akari sighed.","\"You know you can talk to me normally while I’m cooking.\"","\"I know.\"","\"And preferably while maintaining some distance between us.\"","\"...Fine.\"","Noah reluctantly released her.","Akari immediately returned her attention to the food, although the faint blush on her cheeks remained.","Noah leaned comfortably against the wooden wall nearby.","For a while, he simply watched her work.","Then his expression became more thoughtful. \"If we really manage to get out of here...\"","Akari glanced toward him.","\"Hm?\"","\"It’ll only have been around a month and a half in the outside world.\"","\"Approximately, yes.\"","Akari’s expression became slightly complicated.","\"For you.\"","Noah understood immediately.","\"For you, it’ll have been more than twelve years since you disappeared.\"","\"Yes.\"","Silence settled between them for several seconds.","Noah eventually asked, \"What will you do when we get out?\"","Akari’s hands slowed.","\"Me?\"","She thought for a moment.","Then a gentle smile appeared on her face.","\"First...\"","Her blue eyes softened.","\"I’ll find my daughter.\"","Noah remained quiet.","\"I’ll hug Ophelia.\"","Akari’s smile grew warmer.","\"I’ve missed far too much of her life already. I want to see her properly. Talk to her. Hear everything that happened while I was gone.\"","Then her smile suddenly became frighteningly pleasant.","\"And after I’ve finished hugging her...\"","Noah raised an eyebrow.","\"...I’ll give her a very serious scolding for what she did to you.\"","Noah’s eyes immediately brightened.","\"Oh?\"","He straightened slightly.","\"Now that’s wonderful news.\"","Akari chuckled.","\"Don’t look so delighted.\"","\"How can I not?\"","She shook her head helplessly before returning to the soup.","\"After that, I’ll meet Lionel.\"","Noah’s expression became curious.","\"And?\"","\"I’ll officially sever whatever remains of our marriage.\"","There wasn’t much emotion in her voice when she said it.","\"And then I’ll return to my father’s territory in Raigamine.\"","\"Hmm...\"","Noah rubbed his chin thoughtfully.","\"With your current strength, you could probably become the Duchess of the East yourself.\"","Akari glanced toward him with amusement.","\"You think so?\"","\"Of course.\"","Noah smiled.","\"You’re already at the peak of the Sovereign Core. If you successfully awaken your bloodline completely, you’ll probably become even stronger.\"","He folded his arms.","\"Having you as the Duchess of the East would also mean I’d have another incredibly powerful person backing me besides my own family.\"","Akari stared at him for a second. Then she laughed softly.","\"So that’s what you’re thinking about?\"","\"Obviously.\"","\"You really are calculating sometimes.\"","Noah grinned.","\"I’m simply appreciating how fortunate I am.\"","Akari shook her head.","\"You certainly are.\"","---","Later that night.","\"Noah.\"","\"Hmm?\"","\"You’re doing it again.\"","\"I have absolutely no idea what you’re talking about.\" Noah said sleepily.","\"Tch.\"","Akari stared at him with narrowed eyes.","The two were lying beside each other in the room they had shared for months.","And, as had increasingly become his habit, Noah had moved closer after lying down and wrapped an arm around her.","Akari had initially tried to maintain some distance.","As usual. And, as usual. She eventually gave up.","\"Sigh...\"","Her arm reluctantly wrapped around him.","Noah immediately smiled.","Akari noticed. \"Don’t look so pleased with yourself.\"","\"I’m not.\" He replied immediately.","\"You are.\"","\"Hehe~\" He can’t help but giggle.","Akari’s eyes narrowed.","\"Now sleep. And don’t do anything strange. Understood?\"","\"Of course.\"","Noah settled comfortably against her, resting his head against her soft huge chest as his body finally relaxed after another exhausting day of training.","Akari looked down at the young man nestled against her.","Six months ago, she would never have imagined allowing someone to cling to her like this.","Yet now it had somehow become normal. Her expression softened.","She gently placed a hand against the back of Noah’s head, holding him closer as his breathing gradually became slower.","Soon, he was asleep.","Akari watched him quietly for a few moments. Then a faint smile touched her lips.","\"Spoiled child.\"","Despite her words, there wasn’t the slightest trace of annoyance in her voice.","She rested her cheek gently against his snow-white hair and closed her eyes.","Outside, the forest remained peaceful.","And inside the little wooden house, the two slowly drifted to sleep in each other’s warmth.","---","Two Days Later","Noah stood atop a massive rock formation, his blue eyes fixed on the lone figure several hundred meters away.","Akari stood in the center of a vast clearing.","They had deliberately chosen this place because there was nothing nearby except forest and empty land. If Akari lost control, their wooden house would at least remain safe.","More importantly, Noah needed distance. This wasn’t going to be like her previous transformations.","Today, Akari intended to awaken her dragon bloodline completely.","Noah tightened his grip around the sword in his hand.","\"If she loses control...\"","His expression hardened.","He wasn’t strong enough to defeat Akari. That much was obvious. At her current level, she could probably crush him before he even understood what had happened.","His role was simple.","Observe her from a safe distance and intervene only if something went terribly wrong. If she completely lost herself, Noah would try to distract her long enough to help her regain consciousness—or run if there was truly nothing he could do.","Several hundred meters away, Akari slowly inhaled.","Then exhaled. Her eyes closed. The entire forest seemed strangely peaceful.","No birds chirped. No animals moved through the bushes. Even the wind gradually disappeared.","Noah narrowed his eyes.","Akari’s hands slowly clenched.","\"It’s time...\"","She stopped suppressing it.","THUMP!","A powerful heartbeat echoed through the clearing.","Noah’s eyes widened. He had heard it. From hundreds of meters away.","THUMP!","The ground beneath Akari’s feet cracked.","Dark sapphire scales began spreading from her neck, crawling rapidly across her cheeks and down beneath her kimono.","RUMBLE—!","The sky darkened. Massive storm clouds gathered overhead as blue lightning flickered between them.","Noah instinctively took a step backward.","The pressure descending upon the forest was suffocating.","Then Akari’s eyes snapped open. Brilliant blue lightning burned within her vertical pupils.","And she roared.","ROOOOOAAAARRRRR—!!!","It was no longer the voice of a human.","---","[A/N: guys the duchy belonging to Akari’s father is name as Raigamine. I used raiko or something like that name before I guess.. because I thought I haven’t name it. My bad.]"]},{"number":279,"title":"Chapter 279: Run (1)","paragraphs":["THUNDER!!","THUNDER!!!","Brilliant blue lightning tore across the darkened heavens.","The clear sky had disappeared entirely within minutes, swallowed by enormous black storm clouds stretching as far as Noah could see.","WHOOOOOSH!!","Violent winds swept across the forest.","Trees bent beneath the pressure. Branches snapped and flew through the air, while countless leaves were ripped from their stems and scattered into the raging storm.","Noah crossed both arms in front of his face.","\"Argh!\"","His clothes and snow-white hair whipped violently behind him as he struggled to keep his footing.","He narrowed his eyes and forced himself to look toward Akari.","His eyes widened in disbelief.","\"What... the hell...?\"","Noah had already seen Akari’s dragon form countless times over the past six months. Normally, she was around thirty-five meters long from snout to tail.","Already enormous. Already terrifying. But the creature standing before him now was something else entirely.","She had nearly doubled in size. Close to seventy meters of draconic might towered over the forest.","Her four powerful limbs were planted firmly against the earth, each ending in enormous black claws that sank deep into the ground. Her elongated body was covered from head to tail in overlapping dark-sapphire scales, but they were noticeably different from before.","They were darker, thicker and sharper.","Each scale possessed a metallic sheen, reflecting every flash of lightning like polished sapphire armor.","Two enormous black horns extended backward from her head, curving slightly toward the sky. Smaller horn-like spikes formed a jagged ridge down her neck and spine before continuing toward her massive tail.","Her wings slowly spread.","WHOOOOM—!!","Noah’s breath caught.","They were enormous.","The dark-blue membranes stretched between thick skeletal structures, and arcs of electricity continuously danced across their surface.","But the most striking feature was her eyes.","They burned with brilliant electric-blue light.","There was no longer any trace of the calm woman Noah knew within them.","Only the overwhelming presence of a dragon.","Akari raised her enormous head toward the heavens.","Her jaws opened, revealing rows of huge, razor-sharp teeth.","ROOOOOOOOOAAAAARRRRRR—!!!","A deafening, high-pitched draconic roar erupted from her throat.","The sound alone shook the forest.","And immediately afterward.","BOOOOOOM—!!!","An enormous shockwave exploded outward from Akari’s body.","The earth cracked beneath her.","Nearby trees were violently uprooted.","\"SHIT!!\"","Noah barely managed to curse before the shockwave struck him.","WHAM!","His feet left the ground.","He was thrown backward like a broken doll, flying through the air before.","THUD!!","His back slammed painfully against a tree.","\"ARGH!\"","Noah dropped onto one knee.","\"Dammit...\"","His entire back screamed in pain.","Drip.","A cold droplet struck his cheek.","Drip. Drip.","Noah slowly looked upward.","\"...Oh, you’ve got to be kidding me.\"","SHHHHHHH—!!!","Rain suddenly poured from the heavens.","Not ordinary rain.","A violent downpour swept sideways beneath the raging winds, reducing visibility throughout the forest within seconds.","Noah pushed himself upright.","\"I need to get farther away!\"","He was about to run when something above Akari caught his attention.","Crackle—!","Blue electricity appeared around the dragon.","At first, they were only thin arcs.","CRACKLE! CRACKLE!","Thousands of electrical currents began crawling across her enormous body.","Noah froze.","Above Akari, the storm clouds had started rotating. Slowly at first. Then faster. And faster.","A colossal spiral formed directly above the dragon, with Akari standing precisely beneath its center.","Blue lightning continuously flashed within the rotating clouds.","The entire world seemed to alternate between darkness and brilliant blue light.","KRA-KOOOOOOOM—!!!","A gigantic bolt of blue lightning descended.","It struck Akari directly.","Noah’s heart nearly stopped.","But the dragon didn’t scream in pain.","Instead. The lightning spread across her scales.","Another bolt descended.","BOOM!!","Then another.","BOOOOM!!","Again.","Again.","Again.","Noah stared.","\"...They’re not attacking her.\"","His fear slowly transformed into amazement.","The lightning was being absorbed.","Every bolt that struck Akari flowed across her dark-sapphire scales before sinking into her enormous body.","Her horns began glowing. The ridges along her spine illuminated one after another.","Her wings crackled with increasingly violent electricity.","The storm wasn’t attacking the dragon.","It was answering her.","Noah slowly moved behind the thick trunk of a nearby tree, using it as protection from the violent wind.","For several seconds, he simply stared.","His mouth gradually fell open.","\"...Damn.\"","Another colossal bolt struck Akari.","KRAKOOOOM—!!!","The entire forest flashed blue.","Noah’s eyes practically sparkled.","’Man...’","A grin slowly appeared on his face.","’Dragons are so damn cool!’","Any sensible person should probably have been terrified.","Noah certainly had been moments earlier.","But now?","He was watching a seventy-meter Storm Dragon standing beneath a gigantic thunderstorm while absorbing lightning from the heavens.","How was he supposed to not find that amazing?","’Damn it! Now I want to become a dragon too!’","Noah’s grin widened.","’A Frost Dragon would be perfect.’","Then another blast of wind nearly ripped him away from the tree.","\"ARGH—! Okay!\"","Noah desperately grabbed the trunk.","\"Dragons are cool, but I should probably survive this first! It’s not time to admire them.\"","Noah turned around and ran.","He didn’t hesitate for even a second.","Stomp! Stomp! Stomp!","His boots slammed against the damp forest floor as he rushed between the towering trees.","Mana surged through his body, concentrating heavily around his legs and strengthening every muscle. His speed increased dramatically, turning his figure into a pale blur weaving through the dense forest.","’I shouldn’t have come!’","Noah gritted his teeth.","’Why the hell did I insist on staying nearby?!’","He jumped over a fallen tree and landed without slowing down.","’And I definitely didn’t expect her complete awakening to make her that damn huge! Even standing near her is dangerous! Still...’","A small part of him didn’t regret witnessing it.","’After all it’s not every day one get to see a dragon bloodline completely awaken.’","Especially one as powerful as Akari’s.","ROOOOOAAAARRRRR—!!!","The terrifying roar continued behind him, shaking the forest.","Silence.","Noah continued running for several seconds before noticing the sudden change.","\"...Hmm?\"","His pace gradually slowed. The roar had stopped.","There was no thunder nor violent explosions of mana.","’Did she calm down?’","Noah finally stopped.","Breathing heavily, he cautiously turned around.","Despite the enormous distance he had already covered, Akari’s dragon form was still clearly visible above the forest.","She was simply too massive to miss.","Her enormous dark-sapphire wings were spread wide, covering a tremendous expanse.","Lightning occasionally crawled across the edges of her scales, illuminating her gigantic silhouette beneath the storm-darkened sky.","Noah narrowed his eyes.","Flap!","Her wings moved.","FLAP!!","A violent wave of wind exploded outward.","Trees beneath her bent violently. Leaves and broken branches were ripped into the air, while clouds of dust and debris rolled across the forest.","Even from this distance, Noah felt the wind slam against him.","He raised an arm over his face.","’She’s flying.’","Akari’s enormous body slowly rose into the air.","Noah’s tense expression gradually softened.","’Is she... in control?’","He lowered his arm. For several moments, Akari simply remained airborne.","No wild attacks. No uncontrollable destruction. No mindless rampage. A relieved smile slowly appeared on Noah’s face.","\"She did it...\"","His shoulders relaxed.","\"That woman actually did it.\"","She had finally awakened it completely. And apparently retained control.","Noah released a long breath.","\"Thank goodness.\"","Akari’s head moved.","Slowly. Her enormous face turned toward him.","Noah’s smile disappeared.","\"...\"","Her eyes found him.","Ba-dump!","His heart slammed against his chest.","Ba-dump! Ba-dump!","A violent shiver raced down his spine. Every hair on his body stood on end. Noah couldn’t explain it logically.","Akari hadn’t attacked. She hadn’t even moved toward him. Yet every survival instinct inside his body suddenly screamed the same thing.","RUN.","His legs wouldn’t move.","’F-Fuck...’","His pupils trembled.","’Why is she looking at me like that?’","There was nothing familiar in those enormous lightning-blue eyes.","The warmth was gone. There was no recognition.","No trace of the woman who had spent the past months training, eating, laughing, and living beside him.","There was only the gaze of a predator. Akari’s massive jaws slowly opened. Blue lightning flashed between her huge fangs.","Noah’s face paled.","\"Oh, shit—\"","ROOOOOOOOOAAAAARRRRRRR—!!!","The roar exploded across the forest. The sheer force became a physical shockwave.","BOOOOOOM!!!","Trees bent violently. Branches snapped. The ground trembled.","Noah’s body was ripped from the ground and hurled backward.","\"ARGH!\"","He crashed through several bushes before slamming hard against the earth.","Pain shot through his back.","For a second, everything spun.","\"Cough!\"","Noah forced himself onto his hands and knees.","His ears rang.","Warm blood trickled from a small wound near his forehead. But the shock had finally broken the invisible pressure that had frozen his body.","He could move again. Noah looked up. His eyes widened.","Akari’s wings folded slightly.","BOOM!","The air exploded behind her. The gigantic dragon shot forward. Straight toward him.","Noah’s face went completely pale.","\"FUCK!\"","He scrambled onto his feet and immediately ran. Mana violently flooded into his legs.","STOMP!","The earth cracked beneath his first step. Noah shot through the forest at his maximum speed. Behind him, an enormous shadow swept across the trees.","ROOOOOAAAARRRRR!!!","Noah didn’t dare look back.","There was no need. The rapidly growing thunder of beating wings told him everything.","Akari had completely awakened her dragon bloodline. But she hadn’t mastered it. And now she was hunting him."]},{"number":280,"title":"Chapter 280: RUN (2)","paragraphs":["Dammit! Isn’t this too much?!","Noah forced his exhausted legs to move faster as rain hammered against his body.","His clothes were completely drenched, clinging heavily to his skin. His snow-white hair stuck against his forehead while muddy water splashed beneath every frantic step.","’I haven’t even reached the peak of the human ranks yet, and now I have to face a fully awakened dragon?!’","STOMP!","STOMP!","STOMP!","Mana surged violently through his legs.","Noah didn’t care about efficiency anymore.","He poured as much mana as his body could tolerate into physical reinforcement, pushing his speed beyond anything he normally dared to attempt.","’Dragons are walking calamities!’","He gritted his teeth.","’According to myths they can destroy entire cities with a single attack! Some are powerful enough to threaten entire nations! And destroy them in span if few minutes!!’","And here he was. Nineteen years old handsome young man. A Condensed Core mid stage. Running away from one.","’What kind of ridiculous situation is this?!’","CRACKLE—!","Noah’s thoughts abruptly stopped.","Lightning, but this time, it wasn’t coming from the clouds.","\"What now?\"","A terrible sensation crawled across his skin.","Noah looked over his shoulder.","His pupils shrank. The enormous dragon was almost directly above him.","Akari’s gigantic wings stretched across the stormy sky as she pursued him, her sapphire scales illuminated by countless flashes of lightning.","But that wasn’t what terrified Noah.","Her jaws were open.","CRACKLE! CRACKLE! CRACKLE!","Brilliant blue lightning gathered inside her mouth.","It started deep within her throat as a tiny spark before rapidly expanding into a violently compressed sphere of electrical energy.","The surrounding air distorted. Lightning crawled across her fangs. The light became so intense that the inside of her mouth appeared like a miniature blue sun.","Noah’s face lost all color.","’NO!!’","He immediately understood.","’Dragon Breath? Dragon beam? Whatever!!’","\"AKARI!!!\"","Noah screamed with everything his lungs could give him.","\"IT’S ME!\"","His throat burned.","\"NOAH!!\"","For the briefest moment, a foolish part of him hoped she would recognize his voice.","That somewhere beneath those overwhelming draconic instincts, Akari would hear him and remember him.","But those enormous eyes didn’t change. The lightning only grew brighter.","\"Fuck!\"","Noah’s expression collapsed.","’So much for the power of love! I thought it will work!! Was power of love all false?’","There was no miracle coming. No emotional awakening. There was no convenient last-second recognition.","He had only one option.","RUN.","Noah abruptly changed direction. His right foot slammed into the ground.","CRACK!","The earth shattered beneath him as he threw his entire body toward the left.","Mana exploded through his legs. Pain immediately tore through his muscles from the excessive reinforcement.","Noah ignored it. He ran faster. Faster than during his academy training. Faster than during the Wilderness Race. Faster than when monsters had chased him through this forest.","Faster than he had ever run in his entire life. It was run for his survival.Then the world behind him turned blue.","BOOOOOOOOOOOOM—!!!","A colossal beam of concentrated lightning erupted from Akari’s mouth. It tore downward from the heavens like divine punishment.","The beam struck precisely where Noah would’ve been had he continued running straight. For a fraction of a time, there was silence.","KRAAAAAAAAA-BOOOOOOOOM!!!","The forest disappeared in blue-white light.","Lightning exploded outward.","Trees were instantly shattered and incinerated.","The earth collapsed beneath the impact as an enormous crater formed, while countless arcs of electricity tore through the surrounding forest.","Noah had already covered nearly five hundred meters. It wasn’t enough.","\"SHIT!\"","The expanding shockwave reached him.","BOOM—!!!","It struck his back like an invisible mountain.","\"ARGHH!\"","Noah was ripped from the ground.","His body flew forward uncontrollably, smashing through branches before bouncing violently across the muddy earth.","Finally, he crashed through a bush and slammed against the ground.","The entire world shook. The earth trembled as though a massive earthquake had struck the forest.","Trees groaned and collapsed.","Dust, shattered wood, stones, leaves, and debris filled the air, only to be beaten back down by the torrential rain.","Noah lay motionless for several seconds.","\"Cough!\"","Blood splattered from his mouth. His ears rang painfully. His entire back screamed in agony. Yet he was alive.","Noah pushed one trembling hand against the ground.","\"That...\"","He coughed again.","\"woman went crazy!!\"","But Akari wasn’t finished. Far above she was still flying.","ROOOOOAAAARRRRR—!!!","The dragon suddenly shot upward. Her gigantic body disappeared into the dark clouds.","Noah raised his head weakly.","\"What is she...\"","Then his expression changed. The clouds began rotating.","They were slowly at first and then faster and faster.","Akari’s silhouette moved within their depths, occasionally revealed whenever lightning illuminated the heavens.","CRACK!","A massive bolt struck the forest and then another.","CRACK! CRACK!","The storm intensified. Wind screamed between the trees. Rain became so heavy that Noah could barely see more than a few dozen meters ahead.","Lightning spread across the sky in enormous branching webs. The entire region was being swallowed by Akari’s power.","The lakes, the forest and the river everything was covered with rain and storm.","This place, this dimension surely had a boundary. Akari had told him.","It was like an invisible barrier surrounding the hundreds of kilometers huge forest.","And right now that whol dimension was covered by storm.","Even their small wooden house far away was now buried beneath the expanding storm.","Noah stared upward in disbelief. This wasn’t merely bad weather anymore. Akari herself had become the center of the storm.","A living natural disaster. And somewhere within those black clouds. The Storm Dragon continued to roar.","’What should I do? Fuck!’","Noah stood beside a half-broken tree, his back pressed against its cracked trunk as he desperately tried to think.","’For now, I should find somewhere safe and stay hidden... at least until she calms down. But what if she doesn’t? What if she never regains control?’","The thought sent a chill through him.","Noah pushed himself away from the tree, turned, and started running again.","His body was battered and covered in injuries, but thankfully, none of them were severe enough to stop him from running or fighting.","Noah continued running through the forest. His breathing had become ragged, his clothes were soaked with rain, and every muscle in his body screamed from exhaustion. Yet he didn’t dare stop.","CRACK!","A bolt of blue lightning struck somewhere behind him.","BOOM!","The ground trembled beneath his feet.","\"Dammit!\"","Noah pushed through a wall of bushes and suddenly emerged into a familiar clearing.","\"...Huh?\"","His steps slowed.","Noah frowned at the sight before him. In the middle of the forest was a large circular clearing, completely devoid of trees. And at its center stood the same mysterious platform he had discovered during his survival training months ago.","A perfectly circular structure made from some strange gray stone. Ancient runes were carved across its entire surface, forming complicated patterns that Noah still couldn’t understand.","Around the edges of the platform stood several waist-high stone pillars.","And resting atop each one were spherical red crystals. It was familiar place but something was different.","Noah’s eyes narrowed. \"What the hell is happening here?\"","The crystals were glowing. Months ago, they had remained completely lifeless. No matter how much Noah examined them, touched the platform, or poured mana into the runes, nothing had happened.","Pulse.","Red light flashed from every crystal simultaneously.","Then faded.","Pulse.","They flashed again.","Noah stared at them.","\"What...?\"","ROOOOOAAAAARRRRR—!!!","The roar of the Storm Dragon thundered through the forest.","Noah immediately turned. Far above the trees, Akari’s enormous silhouette moved within the raging storm clouds.","Blue lightning spread across the heavens around her.","PULSE!","The crystals suddenly became brighter.","Noah froze.","ROOOOAAARRR—!!","\"No way.\"","Noah’s expression slowly changed. Every time Akari released a powerful surge of energy.","The crystals reacted.","\"This...\"","He cautiously stepped closer.","\"Is this thing reacting to her awakening?\"","His heart began beating faster. Akari had told him that this platform had remained dormant for sixty years. Yet the moment she completely released her dragon bloodline, it suddenly began showing signs of activity.","’Didn’t she notice this things before when she tried to awakened her bloodline? no.. according to her she used to suppress it withing a minute since it was just too hard... so she might have never notice this. Is her awakening activating it?’","Noah stared at the ancient runes.","’Or is it waiting for something?’","Rumble!","The platform suddenly trembled.","Noah immediately stepped backward.","\"What now?!\"","But nothing happened. It was already hard to stand still in such heavy winds despite Noah possessing superhuman powers.","He ran a hand through his hair.","’I have no choice but to try to stay safe... or find some way to help Akari calm down.’","ROOOAAARRR!!","Another thunderous roar tore through the sky. This time, it was much closer.","Noah flinched at the deafening sound and immediately looked up. His eyes widened. The enormous shadow of the dragon could be seen through the dark clouds, passing directly above him.","Then, without warning, she descended. The clouds split apart as something massive came crashing down toward him. Noah saw her leg—or rather, the enormous, razor-sharp claws at the end of it.","’Fuck!’","He didn’t need another warning. Noah shot forward with all his strength."]},{"number":281,"title":"Chapter 281: Enjoying?","paragraphs":["The dragon descended directly toward the section of forest Noah was desperately running through.","FLAP!!","Its enormous wings beat downward.","BOOOOM!!","A violent blast of wind crashed into the forest.","Trees bent beneath the pressure. Some were ripped straight from the earth, their massive roots tearing through the soaked ground before the trunks were hurled aside like twigs. Rainwater exploded from the leaves in clouds of mist, while broken branches and debris scattered everywhere.","Noah threw an arm over his face as he continued running. Fortunately, Akari hadn’t spotted him yet. Or at least, that was what he hoped.","The enormous dragon landed among the trees, its massive claws crushing the earth beneath them.","CRUNCH!!","Several trees shattered beneath its weight.","Then Akari’s dragon form raised its head.","Her jaws slowly opened.","Crackle! Crackle! CRACKLE—!!","Brilliant blue lightning gathered inside her mouth. Arcs of electricity danced between her fangs, growing brighter with every passing second. The air itself seemed to vibrate as an enormous amount of energy condensed within her throat.","Noah’s instincts screamed at him.","’Danger! Danger!’","He immediately turned his head.","\"Shit!!\"","Akari was facing directly toward the path ahead of him.","Noah instantly slammed his foot into the muddy ground and changed direction. Rather than continuing forward, he spun around and sprinted back the way he had come.","At almost the exact same moment.","BOOOOOOOM!!!","A massive beam of blue lightning erupted from the dragon’s mouth.","It tore through the forest.","Trees disappeared within the blinding torrent of electricity. The beam carved a path hundreds of meters long through the woodland, obliterating everything before it.","Noah didn’t dare look back. The explosion that followed shook the earth beneath his feet.","’That would have killed me!’","He continued running until something caught his attention.","Akari’s enormous foreleg.","Because she had descended so low, one of her claws was planted among the trees not far from him.","Noah stared at it.","A reckless idea immediately entered his mind.","’Should I?’","His expression twisted.","’No... that’s fucking idiotic. There is no way power of love or friendship works.’","He took another step. Then glanced at the claw again.","’But...’","Noah clenched his teeth.","\"Fuck it!\"","He abruptly changed direction and dashed toward the dragon.","Mana surged through his body.","Akari’s claw moved through the trees as she adjusted her enormous body, smashing trunks aside without even noticing them.","Noah stretched out his hand.","His ice affinity responded immediately.","Crack! Crack! CRACK!!","Ice erupted beneath his feet. Instead of forming a weapon, Noah continuously created more ice beneath the first layer.The structure rapidly grew upward.","Ten meters, twenty and then thirty meters. A massive pillar of ice rose from the forest floor, carrying Noah toward Akari’s foreleg.","The higher he climbed, the stronger the wind became. Rain struck his face like countless needles.","\"Come on...\"","The pillar reached its limit.","Noah bent his knees. Mana exploded through his legs.","BOOM!","He launched himself from the top. For several terrifying seconds, there was nothing beneath his feet.","There was only wind and rain. And the massive body of a dragon.","\"AAAAHHH!!\"","Noah stretched both arms forward. His fingers struck Akari’s sapphire-blue scales.","They slipped.","\"No!\"","His hand desperately searched for something to grab before finally catching against the raised edge of one enormous scale.","His other hand immediately followed.","BOOOOOOOM!!!","The lightning beam struck the distant forest. A tremendous explosion erupted behind them.","The shockwave swept through the surrounding woodland, throwing smoke, shattered wood, dirt, and vaporized rainwater high into the air.","At the same moment.","FLAP!!!","Akari spread her enormous wings. With one powerful beat, the dragon launched herself back into the sky.","Noah’s stomach dropped.","\"WHOA!!\"","The ground suddenly disappeared beneath him. He tightened his grip with everything he had.","His boots scrambled against Akari’s scales until he managed to find footing along the upper portion of her massive claw.","\"Don’t fall... Don’t fucking fall!\"","He wrapped both arms around the thick lower section of her foreleg.","The scales pressed painfully against his chest and arms. They were harder than steel, with raised edges sharp enough that Noah could feel them scraping against his skin through his clothes.","But he refused to let go. The dragon climbed higher. Wind screamed past him.","His soaked white hair whipped violently behind his head as rain struck his face.","Noah cautiously looked downward.","The forest was rapidly shrinking beneath him.","\"...\"","His heart nearly stopped.","He should have been terrified.","He was terrified.","Yet... A grin slowly spread across his face.","His heart hammered wildly—not entirely from fear anymore.","Adrenaline surged through every part of his body.","He was hundreds of meters above the ground, clinging to the leg of an out-of-control Storm Dragon while lightning ripped across the sky around him.","And somehow he was enjoying it. Noah’s grin widened.","’Fuck... Why am I enjoying this?!’","\"Shit!\"","Despite himself, a laugh escaped his lips as he tightened his grip.","\"Hahaha!\"","Maybe he really had lost his mind.","’It’s time to become a dragon slayer!! Someday, I’ll tell my kids about how I fought a freaking dragon when I was only nineteen!’","---","Noah slowly began climbing. There was no other choice.","Akari’s enormous dragon form continued tearing through the stormy sky, and Noah was still clinging to one of her hind legs.","\"Okay... slowly...\"","His fingers tightened around the edge of a dark sapphire scale.","Crack!","A layer of ice immediately formed around his hand, freezing his palm and fingers against the scale.","Noah had realized something important after nearly being thrown off several times.","His physical strength alone wasn’t enough.","Akari’s scales were smooth in some places and sharply raised in others. Combined with the rain and the violent wind rushing against him, maintaining a normal grip was nearly impossible.","So he used his Ice Creation differently.","Every time he grabbed onto a scale, Noah formed a layer of ice around his hand and the scale beneath it, temporarily locking them together.","Then, when he needed to move.","Crack!","He shattered the ice. Reached higher. Grabbed another scale.","Crack!","And froze his hand in place again. It wasn’t fast. But it worked.","---","[A/N: Bear with me, guys... I’m still planning a few things, so please bear with Chapters like this for a little while longer. The main stuff is coming soon!]"]},{"number":282,"title":"Chapter 282: Haha!! I made it!!","paragraphs":["\"Come on...\"","Noah pulled himself upward. His boots desperately searched for gaps between the enormous scales.","ROOOOOAAAAARRRRR!!!","Akari’s roar ripped through the heavens. The sheer vibration traveled through her entire body.","\"Argh!\"","Noah’s teeth rattled. Then she accelerated.","BOOM!","The dragon tore through the air with such force that the clouds around her were blown apart.","\"FUCK!!\"","Noah flattened himself against her body. His arms screamed from the strain.","Wind battered him relentlessly while rain struck his skin like tiny projectiles He couldn’t even properly open his eyes.","Still, he continued.","One scale, then another and then another.","Akari’s hind leg alone was enormous. Noah felt less like he was climbing a living creature and more like he was scaling the side of some moving fortress.","His progress was painfully slow. But eventually, he reached the upper portion of her leg.","\"Almost...\"","Noah reached upward.","ROOOOOAAAARRR!!","Suddenly, Akari’s entire body jerked violently. Her wings lost their rhythm.","\"What the—?!\"","The dragon abruptly twisted sideways. The entire world rotated around Noah.","\"FUCK! I’M GOING TO FALL!!\"","His feet lost their grip. For one horrifying second, his entire body was hanging from a single arm.","Noah immediately released a burst of mana.","CRACK!","Ice spread around his hand, locking his fingers firmly against one of Akari’s scales.","\"ARGHH!\"","His shoulder screamed under the weight of his entire body. He desperately swung his free hand upward.","Grabbed another scale. Froze it.","Then pulled himself back against her body.","\"Hah... hah...\"","His breathing was wild.","\"What the hell was that?!\"","Then Noah noticed something strange.","Akari wasn’t simply flying erratically. Her movements had changed. Her enormous head jerked to one side.","Her claws curled inward. One wing suddenly folded slightly before immediately spreading again.","She shook her head violently.","ROOOAARR—!!","But this roar sounded different. There was something almost painful about it.","Noah’s eyes widened.","’Wait.’","He stared toward her distant head.","She’s fighting.","Akari wasn’t completely gone.","Somewhere beneath those awakened draconic instincts, the woman he knew was still struggling to regain control of her own body.","A small spark of hope appeared in Noah’s eyes.","She’s still in there. Then this isn’t hopeless.","Noah gritted his teeth and resumed climbing.","\"Akari!\"","His voice was immediately swallowed by the storm.","’Of course.’","From this far away, there was no chance she could hear him.","He needed to get closer.","Much closer.","’Time to show power of love!!’","---","It took Noah several exhausting minutes to reach Akari’s back.","The moment he pulled himself over the final row of scales, he collapsed flat against her enormous body.","\"Hah... hah...\"","He desperately sucked air into his lungs.","His arms were trembling.","Several cuts covered his palms and forearms where the sharp edges of Akari’s scales had scraped him whenever his ice grip failed.","But there was no time to rest.","Noah raised his head.","Akari’s back stretched before him like a massive sapphire road, leading all the way toward the base of her neck.","Beyond that was her enormous head.","Noah swallowed.","’I need to reach her ear.’","It sounded absurd even inside his own head.","He was going to crawl across the back of an awakened dragon, reach her head, and try to talk some sense into her.","This might genuinely be the stupidest thing I’ve ever done.","CRACK!!!","Lightning tore through the clouds only a short distance away.","Noah flinched.","\"...Still better than letting her destroy the entire forest.\"","He pushed himself forward. Walking normally was impossible. Akari’s body constantly tilted and shifted beneath him with every beat of her wings.","So Noah remained low. Almost crawling. One hand moved forward.","Crack!","Ice locked it against a scale. Then the other.","Crack!","His knees and boots followed.","He essentially created temporary anchors across Akari’s body, breaking each one only after securing the next.","It was slow and exhausting. But far safer than relying on his grip alone.","FLAP—!!!","Akari’s wings beat downward.","Noah’s body was almost ripped away.","\"Argh!\"","He flattened himself against her back.","\"Would you stop moving for five damn seconds?!\"","As if answering him.","ROOOOOAAAARRR!!!","\"No?! Fine!\"","Noah continued crawling.","Akari suddenly plunged downward.","Noah’s stomach rose into his throat. \"Hehe! This is crazy....but also there’s slight fun.\"","Then she shot upward again. Clouds swallowed them. Everything became gray.","Rain and mist blinded Noah completely.","Lightning flashed around them.","CRACK!","For several few seconds, Noah couldn’t see anything beyond the scales directly beneath his face.","Yet he continued moving.","’I need her conscious.’","That mysterious platform was still bothering him. For sixty years, it had remained dormant. Then Akari fully awakened her bloodline.","And suddenly the crystals had begun glowing. The runes had activated. Something was happening.","And Noah didn’t want to discover what it was while Akari remained a rampaging dragon incapable of thinking clearly.","Their house was probably already destroyed. The forest was being devastated. If this continued, there might not be much of this place left.","\"Akari...\"","Noah pulled himself farther.","\"You better wake up after everything I’m doing!\"","Another violent movement nearly threw him away.","CRACK!","Ice immediately spread from both palms.","Noah held on.","His mana reserves were steadily decreasing, but fortunately these small amounts of ice required far less mana than creating large structures or using combat spells.","So he continued.","Grab, then freeze and then pull.","After that Break.","Again, again and again he did the same thing. Minutes felt like hours. His fingers became numb. His shoulders burned.","His breathing grew heavier. But gradually, the massive base of Akari’s neck came closer.","Finally Noah reached forward and grabbed one of the thick scales there.","Crack!","He froze both hands firmly against it. Then dragged himself forward.","\"ARGHH!\"","With one final pull, Noah climbed onto the base of Akari’s neck.","He immediately pressed his entire body against her scales.","\"Hah... hah... hah...\"","For a while, he couldn’t move.","He had made it. \"Hahaha!! I made it!!\"","From here, Akari’s enormous head was finally within reachable distance.","Noah slowly raised his face.","Her horns stretched backward above him while lightning danced across the clouds surrounding her enormous silhouette.","Her head violently shifted from side to side as she continued fighting whatever instincts had overwhelmed her mind.","Noah clenched his aching fingers.","\"Alright...\"","He stared toward the side of her head.","\"Now I just need to reach your ear.\"","His lips twitched bitterly.","\"...Without getting myself killed.\"","But a smile unknowingly formed on his face.","Slowly Noah was developing liking to something that he shouldn’t.","----","[A/N: Finally I felt like Noah is suffering little bit... but this is not enough. I am not satisfied. I need to beat his ass more Hahaha!!!]"]},{"number":283,"title":"Chapter 283: AKARI!!! IT’S ME! NOAH!! YOUR MAN!!","paragraphs":["\"AKARI!!\"","Noah screamed at the top of his lungs while desperately climbing farther up her enormous neck. His voice was almost completely swallowed by the raging storm.","CRACK!!","Lightning tore across the blackened sky.","ROOOOOAAAARRRRR!!!","Akari answered with a deafening roar. Her massive head suddenly swung to the side, dragging her long neck along with it.","\"WHOA!!\"","Noah’s entire body was nearly thrown away. His stomach twisted violently as the world spun around him.","\"Wait! Listen to me!!\"","Of course, she didn’t. Whether she couldn’t hear him or simply couldn’t understand him in her current state, Noah had no idea.","Akari abruptly changed direction again.","FLAP!!","Her enormous wings pushed against the storm. The sudden acceleration nearly ripped Noah from her neck.","\"ARGH!\"","His fingers screamed in pain. His right hand slipped.","\"No!\"","Noah immediately slammed it against another scale. Mana rushed toward his palm.","Crack!","Ice formed instantly, spreading around his fingers and locking his hand firmly against the sapphire scale. Only then did he release his left hand.","Reach farther and grab then freeze.","Crack!","Then repeat.","His method was crude, but it was the only reason he hadn’t fallen to his death.","Rainwater constantly streamed over Akari’s scales, making them dangerously slippery. The violent wind battered Noah from every direction, while every movement of the dragon threatened to fling him hundreds of meters toward the forest below.","His fingers had become raw.","Several nails were cracked.","His arms trembled from exhaustion, and his shoulders felt as though someone were slowly tearing the muscles apart.","Still, Noah refused to stop.","\"Akari!\"","He dragged himself another meter forward.","\"You better wake the hell up after I went through all this!\"","ROOOAARRR!!","\"Yeah, yeah! Keep roaring!\"","Noah gritted his teeth.","\"I’m still coming!\"","---","Meanwhile, far below the raging storm. The mysterious circular platform remained completely deserted.","Rain poured across its ancient gray surface. Yet the water couldn’t settle upon it.","Something had changed.","Hum","A faint vibration passed through the structure. The red crystals resting atop the waist-high pillars had stopped blinking.","Instead they now remained illuminated. A deep crimson glow burned steadily within each crystal. Then the runes began changing.","Starting from the outermost edge of the platform, an unknown red substance or perhaps some unknown energy slowly seeped through the engraved lines.","It moved almost like liquid. One carved symbol after another turned crimson.","The energy traveled through the intricate channels, gradually connecting separate sections of the enormous formation.","Rumble.","The platform trembled. But it was only for a second. Then everything became still again. But the process didn’t stop.","More runes awakened. More lines filled with crimson light.","The strange energy leaking from them gradually became denser, rising a few centimeters above the stone like thin red mist before dissolving into the air.","Whatever the platform was doing. It wasn’t fully activated yet. It was preparing.","As though an ancient mechanism that had remained dormant for decades was finally awakening from its sleep. And with every passing minute, more of the formation turned red.","---","CRACK—!!!","Another bolt of lightning illuminated the heavens.","Noah barely noticed anymore.","\"Hah... hah...\"","His breaths came in ragged gasps. He had lost track of how long he’d been climbing.","Five minutes? Ten? Twenty?","It felt like hours. His entire body was aching.","His forearms were covered in cuts from Akari’s scales. His wet clothes had torn in several places, and every muscle from his fingers to his back burned from constantly holding himself against the dragon.","But finally Noah looked up. His exhausted eyes widened.","\"I made it.\"","Akari’s enormous head was right there. No longer some distant shape at the end of her neck.","He had reached it.","Her long horns stretched backward above him, and the scales surrounding the back of her skull were larger and thicker than those covering her neck.","Noah could even see the side of her enormous blue eye whenever she turned her head.","He slowly dragged himself farther forward.","\"Just... a little more...\"","His right hand reached out.","Crack!","Ice secured his grip. Then his left. His body followed. Akari suddenly shook her head again.","\"Fuck!\"","Noah immediately flattened himself against her scales. His vision spun. For a moment, nausea surged through his stomach.","\"Ugh...\"","He swallowed it back.","’Not now.’","Once Akari’s movements became slightly steadier, Noah raised his head again. He looked toward the side of her skull. Her ear.","That was his target. Getting there wouldn’t magically solve everything.","Noah knew that.","Akari was in a berserk state caused by the complete awakening of her bloodline. Simply screaming her name might accomplish absolutely nothing.","But he had to try. Because he had seen her fighting against herself earlier. Some part of Akari was still conscious. Somewhere inside that enormous dragon...","His master was still there. Noah clenched his bleeding fingers against her scales.","\"Just wait, Akari...\"","Despite the pain, he forced himself forward again.","\"I’m coming.\"","---","\"Haha!! I finally made it!!\"","Noah shouted triumphantly, though his celebration was immediately ruined when Akari violently shook her enormous head from side to side.","\"Whoa—! Stop! STOP!\"","His frozen grip barely kept him attached to her scales. He had finally reached her ear. Taking a deep breath, Noah screamed with everything he had.","\"AKARI!!! IT’S ME! NOAH!! YOUR MAN!!\"","For a moment Akari actually stopped. Her enormous wings continued beating, but the violent shaking ceased.","Noah’s eyes widened.","\"Akari...?\"","ROOOOOAAARRR—!!!","A deafening roar erupted from her throat. But this time, it sounded different. Painful and strained. As though something inside her was desperately fighting for control.","Noah immediately understood. \"YOU CAN HEAR ME, CAN’T YOU?!\"","Akari growled. \"YOU CAN DO IT! CONTROL IT!!\"","He tightened his grip. \"AFTER THIS, WE CAN FINALLY FIND A WAY OUT OF HERE!\"","ROOOAARRR!!","Her roar almost sounded like a response.","\"It’s working...\"","Noah grinned.","\"COME ON, AKARI!\"","Suddenly the world flipped.","\"What the—?!\"","Akari turned completely upside down. Noah’s stomach lurched as his body hung beneath her neck, held only by his frozen grip.","\"Fuck!\"","Then something in the distance caught his attention. Several kilometers away, visible even through the rain and darkness. A brilliant crimson light illuminated the forest.","Noah’s eyes widened.","\"The platform...?\"","It was glowing. Not faintly anymore. Bright red energy rose from the clearing like a beacon.","\"What the fuck is happening there?\"","RUMBLE—!!!","The clouds above Akari suddenly churned. Lightning gathered throughout the storm.","Noah looked upward. His face paled.","\"Oh, shit.\"","Dozens of enormous lightning bolts descended toward Akari simultaneously.","’If those hit her while I’m attached...’","\"I’m dead!\"","Noah looked toward Akari’s head one last time.","\"AKARI!! WAKE UP!!\" He called her one last time. Then he shattered the ice around his hands and let go.","WHOOSH!!","His body immediately plummeted. Wind screamed around him as Noah fell toward the distant forest like a cannonball, his white hair whipping violently behind him.","Yet even while falling, his eyes remained fixed on that mysterious crimson light."]},{"number":284,"title":"Chapter 284: New Problem","paragraphs":["High above the forest, Akari hovered within the heart of the storm. Her enormous wings beat steadily, each movement generating powerful gusts that tore through the surrounding clouds.","RUMBLE!!","The dark-gray clouds began spiraling around her once again. Blue lightning flashed endlessly within them, illuminating her massive sapphire body.","Then Akari’s eyes suddenly glowed brighter.","ROOOOOAAAAARRRRR!!!","Her roar shook the heavens and the storm answered.","CRACK! CRACK! CRACK!","Dozens of lightning bolts converged upon her from every direction. They didn’t simply strike her. They remained connected.","Continuous streams of lightning wrapped around Akari’s wings, horns, scales, and enormous body as though the dragon were forcibly drawing the entire storm into herself.","Her sapphire scales began glowing from within. Every second, more lightning poured into her.","Far below Noah was still falling. His wet white hair whipped violently above his head as gravity dragged him toward the forest. Yet his eyes remained fixed on Akari.","’She’s... absorbing the lightning again? But it’s too much this time.’","For a moment, amazement overwhelmed him. Then Noah’s expression changed.","’This isn’t the time to be impressed!’","He twisted his body in midair until he was facing downward. The forest was approaching quickly.","Noah stretched out his hand. His frost-blue eyes glowed.","\"Come on...\"","Mana poured from his body.","CRACK!","Cold mist erupted beneath him. Ice rapidly condensed in the empty air, expanding outward until an enormous three-meter-long sword formed below his falling body.","Noah had been practicing this for only a few weeks. Flying using his Ice Creation. Until now, he had only practiced under controlled conditions.","Trying it beside Akari’s enormous dragon form would’ve been suicidal. The wind generated by a single flap of her wings could easily destroy his balance.","But right now he didn’t have another option.","THUD!","Noah landed heavily on the broad surface of the ice sword. His knees bent from the impact, and both hands slammed against the frozen surface to keep himself from tumbling off. The sword immediately dropped several meters under his added weight.","\"Whoa!\"","Noah poured more mana into it. The descent gradually slowed. Then it stopped.","\"Hah...\"","Noah slowly stood.","\"It’s still difficult...\"","Controlling thirty floating weapons was one thing. Controlling a single object while standing on it was completely different.","His own weight constantly affected the sword’s movement and balance. Every small shift of his body changed its center of gravity.","And the storm made everything worse. Wind pushed against him. Rain made the surface slippery. Even a sudden turn could throw him off.","Noah solved at least one problem immediately.","Crack!","Ice spread over his boots, temporarily fastening them to the sword.","\"This is better.\"","He leaned forward slightly.","\"Alright... move.\"","The sword accelerated.","Whoosh!","It was not particularly fast. But it was fast enough for him to reach there.","Noah kept his knees slightly bent, lowering his center of gravity while continuously adjusting the sword with his Ice Creation.","Behind him, the entire forest flashed blue as Akari continued absorbing an unbelievable amount of lightning.","Noah didn’t look back again. His attention remained fixed on the crimson light ahead. The closer he got, the worse the feeling in his chest became.","’Something is wrong. Very wrong.’ He thought tensely.","Finally, the clearing became visible.","Noah’s eyes widened.","\"Shit.\"","The circular platform was no longer merely glowing. A massive crimson portal had formed above it. Red energy rotated violently within its center, resembling a vortex of blood-colored light.","And things were coming through. Creatures continuously crawled and leaped from the portal onto the platform.","Noah recognized them immediately. His face hardened.","\"No fucking way...\"","The pale, grotesque bodies. The unnatural limbs. The same horrifying appearance.","’They’re the monsters from the dungeon in Novaris city.’","The same creatures he and Damien had encountered. Fear crawled across Noah’s skin.","\"Why are they coming out here?\"","Then he noticed something worse. Thin streams of crimson energy were leaking from the portal. One touched the grass.","Hisssss","The grass blackened almost instantly. Another strand brushed against a nearby tree. Its bark cracked. The leaves withered. Within seconds, an entire section of the trunk began decaying into a dark, lifeless mass.","Noah’s expression turned grim.","\"What the hell is that energy?\"","Whatever it was, he had absolutely no intention of touching it. He remained more than forty meters above the ground.","SCREEEEEECH!!!","Several monsters looked upward. Their distorted faces locked onto Noah. Then one of them screamed. The others immediately followed.","SCREECH!","SCREEEEEECH!!","\"Great.\"","Noah raised his hand.","\"You noticed me.\"","The monsters gathered beneath him. Noah’s eyes glowed frost-blue. Mana surged outward. Cold mist suddenly filled the sky.","Crack! Crack! Crack!","One ice weapon appeared. Then another. And another.","Swords, spears, daggers and axes. More than sixty weapons formed in the air around Noah, suspended above the clearing like a frozen arsenal.","Months ago, controlling this many would’ve demanded his full concentration. Now his control was considerably better. Noah lowered his hand.","’Fall.’","The weapons descended.","WHOOSH!!!","Sixty blades rained from the sky.","THUD! THUD! THUD!","Ice spears punched through shoulders and chests. Swords pierced skulls. Several creatures were pinned directly against the stone platform. Others managed to move at the last moment, suffering deep wounds instead of fatal ones.","But Noah wasn’t finished. His hand closed into a fist.","\"Break.\"","CRACK!!!","Every embedded weapon shattered. The fragments didn’t scatter harmlessly.","Noah maintained control over the ice. The broken pieces rapidly reshaped themselves into dozens of razor-sharp spikes before exploding outward.","SHRK! SHRK! SHRK!","The monsters were torn apart from within and around. Blood splattered across the ground. Bodies collapsed one after another.","Noah watched from above, breathing steadily. But his expression didn’t relax.","Because behind the corpses.","SCREEECH!!!","More creatures crawled through the portal. Then more behind them. And more. Noah’s eyes slowly narrowed.","\"...They’re not stopping.\"","The portal continued rotating. Crimson energy continued leaking into the forest. And somewhere above him, the Storm Dragon continued gathering lightning.","Noah tightened his fists.","\"This is getting worse by the second.\""]},{"number":285,"title":"Chapter 285: Deal with something completely unknown","paragraphs":["Noah continued staring at the enormous crimson portal. More monsters poured out without pause.","One after another, their grotesque white bodies emerged from the swirling red surface before scattering into the surrounding forest.","Noah’s expression grew increasingly grim.","\"What should I do...?\"","He rubbed his forehead in frustration.","\"Dammit. This is way beyond me.\"","He had no idea what the platform was, why it had suddenly activated, or why the same creatures from the labyrinth were now emerging from it.","’Once again, I have to deal with something completely unknown.’","Noah clicked his tongue.","’Damn it! I’m seriously jealous of those transmigrators who remember every single event from the future.’","He possessed no knowledge about the game. And right now, complaining wouldn’t solve anything.","Noah took a deep breath.","\"Fine.\"","His eyes narrowed at the platform below.","\"Let’s get closer first. Maybe there’s some way to deactivate it.\"","The massive ice sword beneath his feet slowly tilted forward. Noah concentrated.","Whoosh!","It began moving toward the clearing.","He deliberately kept his speed low. Flying faster would only make controlling the sword more difficult, and the last thing he wanted was to lose his balance and fall directly into that strange crimson energy.","Soon, he passed above the portal itself.","Noah looked down.","\"...That’s disturbing.\"","The portal stretched horizontally across most of the circular platform like a massive pool of swirling crimson energy.","From above, he could clearly see creatures forcing themselves through its surface. Hands appeared first. Then heads. Then entire bodies crawled free.","SCREEECH!!","Some immediately charged into the forest, while others wandered around the platform as though searching for prey.","Noah’s gaze moved toward the edges.","’There.’","One section of the forest beside the clearing was relatively empty. Most of the monsters seemed interested in spreading outward rather than remaining close to the portal.","\"Good enough.\"","Noah guided his sword toward it. The ice blade gradually descended between the trees.","Thud!","The sword touched the muddy ground. Noah immediately jumped off. The moment his boots landed on the soil, he released his control.","Crack!","The enormous sword shattered into hundreds of tiny ice fragments before dissolving into cold mist.","Noah straightened himself. From here, the situation looked even worse.","SCREECH!","ROAR!!","Monster cries echoed continuously through the forest. The crimson glow from the portal illuminated the trees, mixing strangely with the blue flashes of Akari’s storm above.","Noah cautiously moved forward. He didn’t draw his sword yet.","Instead, his mana circulated continuously through his body, ready to respond the instant something attacked him.","Rustle!","Noah’s head snapped toward his right. One of the pale creatures burst through the bushes.","Its red eyes immediately locked onto him.","\"Of course.\"","The creature lunged. Noah didn’t even stop walking. He casually raised his right hand.","Crack!","An ice sword formed beside him.","With a flick of his fingers.","Whoosh!","The sword shot forward like an arrow.","SHRK!","It pierced directly through the monster’s skull. The creature’s body was thrown backward before crashing onto the ground.","Thud!","It was dead.","Noah glanced at it only briefly. These individual creatures weren’t the problem anymore. Not after how much stronger he had become.","His eyes returned to the enormous crimson portal.","\"The problem...\"","His expression became serious.","\"...is that thing.\"","No matter how many monsters he killed, more would simply replace them. So Noah continued toward the platform. He needed to find the source.","And somehow he needed to shut it down.","The strange crimson energy continued leaking from the portal.","Wherever it touched, destruction followed.","Grass withered and dissolved. Tree bark blackened before slowly crumbling away. Even the soil seemed to lose its vitality, turning dark and lifeless beneath the spreading energy.","Noah cautiously moved closer.","His attention shifted toward the stone pillars surrounding the circular platform. The crystal orbs resting atop them were still glowing bright red.","’What if I destroy those?’","It was the most obvious solution. Perhaps the crystals were supplying energy to the portal—or acting as anchors keeping it open.","\"Only one way to find out.\"","Noah extended his hand.","Crack!","A long spear of condensed ice formed beside him. He aimed directly at the nearest crystal.","\"Go.\"","WHOOSH!","The spear shot forward like an arrow, leaving a clean blue trail behind it.","THUD!!","It struck the crystal dead center. The ice spear shattered instantly.","Noah’s eyes widened.","\"What?\"","He stared at the crystal. There wasn’t even a scratch.","\"...Is it really that hard?\"","His expression darkened. ’What am I supposed to do?’","SCREEECH!!","Noah turned. Another horde of monsters was rushing toward him. Twenty of them or perhaps more.","Normally, Noah would’ve prepared himself for battle.","But right now he was irritated. His frost-blue eyes suddenly began glowing. His expression became blank. The frustration disappeared. Then the fear. Then the hesitation.","One emotion after another faded until only an unnatural coldness remained.","[Monarch’s Decree]","An invisible pressure descended upon the clearing. The charging creatures suddenly stopped. Their bodies trembled. Several instinctively lowered themselves. They were weaker than Noah.","And before the authority carried within his bloodline, their instincts screamed only one thing.","Noah raised one hand. The earth beneath the monsters froze.","CRACK!","Dozens of thin, needle-like ice spikes erupted upward.","SHRK! SHRK! SHRK!","They tore through flesh. The entire group was impaled almost simultaneously, their bodies lifted from the ground upon a forest of bloody ice needles.","Noah didn’t even look at them again. A sword appeared in his hand.","\"If attacking from a distance doesn’t work...\"","He stared at the nearest crystal.","\"I’ll do it directly.\"","He stepped forward. Immediately, the pressure coming from the portal intensified.","Noah stopped.","’Can I even approach that thing without being harmed?’","The crimson energy was clearly dangerous. He wasn’t stupid enough to test it with his bare skin. Cold mana surged from his core.","Crack! Crack!","Ice spread upward from his boots, across his legs, from his waist, chest and arms. Within seconds, Noah had covered almost his entire body in a thin layer of protective ice."]},{"number":286,"title":"Chapter 286: I am absolutely not fighting that thing!","paragraphs":["\"Just in case.\"","He continued forward. A thin stream of crimson energy drifted toward him. The moment it touched his ice.","HISSSSS","Noah’s eyes narrowed. The ice began dissolving. It was not melting.","’Eroding.’","\"Shit.\"","He immediately supplied more mana.","Crack!","Fresh ice replaced the destroyed layer. Another stream struck his shoulder.","Hissss!","More ice disappeared. Noah restored it again.","’So it can eat through mana-created ice too.’","That was bad. But Noah kept moving.","SCREECH!","A monster rushed toward him from the side. Noah swung once.","Slash!","Its head separated from its body. Another came from behind. Without turning, Noah conjured an ice blade.","Whoosh!","The weapon shot backward and pierced straight through its chest.","Noah continued walking. The closer he got, the heavier the atmosphere became. It felt as though invisible weight was being placed upon his shoulders.","His breathing gradually changed.","\"Hah...\"","Then took Another step.","\"Hah... hah...\"","His instincts screamed at him to retreat. The energy surrounding the portal felt fundamentally wrong. Still, Noah forced himself forward.","\"Almost...\"","Suddenly a wave of crimson energy surged from the portal. Noah’s eyes widened. He instinctively turned his head away.","WHOOSH!","Most of it passed beside him. But a tiny strand brushed across his exposed cheek.","\"ARGHHH!!\"","Noah stumbled backward. His hand immediately shot toward his face. Pain exploded across his cheek. It didn’t feel like burning. It was worse. It felt as though the flesh itself was being rapidly decomposed.","\"Fuck!\"","Noah pulled his hand away. A dark, sticky patch had appeared across his cheek where the energy had touched him. The upper layer of skin had partially broken down, leaving behind an ugly, raw wound.","His stomach twisted.","\"What the hell is this energy...?\"","Noah immediately covered himself more thoroughly.","CRACK!","Ice spread across his neck and face, forming a crude helmet that left only narrow openings around his eyes and nose. He tightened his grip on his sword.","Mana flowed into the blade. A thin layer of highly compressed frost formed along its edge, sharpening it further while Noah reinforced the weapon with mana.","\"One attack.\"","He stared at the crystal.","\"I’ll put everything into it.\"","He stepped forward.","SCREEECH!!","Another creature charged him. Noah didn’t even turn. An ice sword materialized beside his shoulder.","WHOOSH!","It shot past him.","SHRK!","The monster collapsed with the weapon buried through its skull. Noah reached the pillar. He planted his feet. Both hands wrapped around his sword.","Mana surged through his arms, shoulders, waist, and legs. The blade glowed intensely.","\"BREAK!!\"","Noah swung with everything he had.","CLAAAAANG!!!","A violent shockwave exploded outward. Dust and dead leaves were blasted away. The stone beneath Noah’s boots cracked from the force transferred through his body.","His arms went numb. The vibration traveled from the blade into his wrists, through his elbows, and all the way into his shoulders.","\"Argh!\"","Noah staggered backward. He stared at the crystal. His breathing stopped.","\"...No.\"","Not even a crack. Not even a tiny chip. There wasn’t so much as a scratch upon its glowing red surface. Noah’s expression finally changed from frustration...","To horror his strongest direct strike hadn’t done anything. Behind the crystal, the crimson portal continued to churn. More monsters crawled through.","More corruptive energy leaked outward. And the red orb continued glowing as though Noah had never touched it. Noah tightened his trembling fingers around his sword.","\"...What the hell am I supposed to do now?\"","Unfortunately for Noah, his luck had always been terrible. Just as he was desperately thinking of another way to destroy the crystals—","GRRRRRRROOOOOOOWL!!!","A deep growl emerged from the portal. Noah froze on his position. It wasn’t like the screeches of the monsters he had been slaughtering.","This sound was deeper and heavier. The growl seemed to come from somewhere unimaginably far beyond the crimson portal, yet its vibrations still traveled through the entire clearing.","Noah slowly turned his head. His frost-covered face became tense. Despite the cold armor covering his body, a chill crawled across his skin.","GRRRRROOOOOOOOWL!!!","The portal trembled. Noah took a step backward. Then another. His instincts were screaming.","They were not warning him to prepare for battle, not telling him to defend himself. They were giving him one simple command.","RUN.","’Something dangerous is coming.’","Noah’s eyes widened.","\"Fuck...\"","He didn’t hesitate. \"I need to get out of here!\"","Noah turned and dashed away.","BOOM!","Mana exploded through his legs as he sprinted toward the forest. Behind him the crimson portal distorted. Its surface bulged outward.","Then something emerged. Five enormous fingers slowly pushed through the portal.","They were blackish-red in color, covered in distorted, decaying flesh. Some sections looked burned while others appeared rotten and swollen. But what made the sight truly horrifying were the things embedded within that flesh.","Monsters, dozens of them, their faces, their arms. Half-formed bodies.","The same pale creatures Noah had been fighting were seemingly fused directly into the gigantic hand, their bodies merged together as though they were nothing more than pieces of flesh used to construct something larger.","Some of their heads were still moving. Their mouths opened soundlessly. The enormous hand continued emerging.","It was so large that a single finger was comparable to the trunk of an ancient tree.","BOOOOOOM!!!","The hand crashed down outside the platform. Several enormous trees disappeared beneath its palm. The earth shook violently.","Noah nearly lost his footing.","\"What the hell?!\"","He looked over his shoulder while running. And immediately regretted it. The ground beneath the creature’s hand was changing.","HISSSSSSS","Grass withered instantly. Trees blackened. Their leaves collapsed into dark sludge before their trunks began rotting away.","Even the soil itself seemed to decay, turning black and lifeless as the corruption rapidly spread outward from wherever the hand touched.","Noah’s eyes widened in horror. The smaller streams of crimson energy had taken time to erode things. This was different. The creature itself carried that corruption.","Anything it touched simply died. Noah faced forward again.","\"Nope!\"","Mana surged harder through his legs.","\"I am absolutely not fighting that thing!\"","Behind him, the gigantic fingers dug into the earth.","CRUNCH!!","The arm tightened. As though whatever existed on the other side of the portal. Was beginning to pull the rest of its body through."]},{"number":287,"title":"Chapter 287: Run or Fight?","paragraphs":["Noah kept running. He didn’t dare slow down.","Mana surged continuously through his legs as he pushed his exhausted body farther away from the portal.","Behind him was a chaos.","BOOOOOOM!!!","Another enormous arm erupted from the crimson vortex. Its gigantic palm slammed onto the opposite side of the clearing.","The impact shook the entire forest. Trees snapped. The ground split apart. Dust, rotten vegetation, and broken pieces of wood exploded into the air.","GWRRROOOOOOOOOOWL!!!","Noah’s blood ran cold. Something was pulling itself out. The two massive hands dug into the earth, fingers sinking deep into the soil.","Then the creature pushed. Slowly something enormous began rising from the portal.","RUMBLE.","The earth trembled. Lightning flashed across the storm-filled heavens. For a single instant, the brilliant blue light illuminated the creature completely.","And an enormous shadow fell across the forest.","BOOM!","An overwhelming pressure descended.","Noah’s eyes widened.","\"Argh!\"","His legs suddenly buckled. One knee slammed into the muddy ground.","\"What... the hell...?\"","It wasn’t a physical attack. It was simply the pressure released by the creature’s existence.","Ba-dump!","Noah’s heart hammered violently.","Ba-dump!","Every instinct within his body screamed at him to escape. But curiosity—and perhaps disbelief—forced Noah to look back.","His pupils contracted.","\"...Fuck.\"","An abomination had emerged halfway through the portal. Its body was vaguely humanoid.","Only vaguely. From its waist to the top of its head, the creature stood nearly forty meters tall—and its lower body hadn’t even emerged yet.","Its entire form consisted of the same disgusting blackish-red flesh as its arms. But that flesh wasn’t truly its own.","Hundreds of creatures appeared to have been fused together to construct its body. Arms protruded randomly from its torso.","Half-formed heads were embedded within its shoulders and chest. Faces stretched across its flesh, some frozen in silent screams while others twitched unnaturally.","Noah felt his stomach turn.","\"What kind of fucking monster is that...?\"","Its head was even worse. There were no recognizable features except for a mouth.","And one enormous eye. The eye opened.","Squelch.","Wet flesh peeled apart around it. A gigantic blood-red eye stared across the forest, its surface filled entirely with crimson except for a single pitch-black pupil at the center.","Noah couldn’t explain why but the moment that eye opened, he felt incredibly small.","Like an insect standing before something that shouldn’t exist. Around the portal, the corruption intensified.","HISSSSSSS","Trees withered. Grass disappeared.","The earth blackened. Even stones began cracking and crumbling beneath the spreading crimson energy.","Within seconds, dozens of meters surrounding the platform had become completely lifeless. Then something else happened.","The pale monsters stopped moving. Every single one. The creatures that had previously been pouring endlessly from the portal suddenly turned toward the massive abomination.","None attacked it. None fled. Instead, they lowered their grotesque bodies. Almost like subjects kneeling before their king.","Noah’s expression became grim.","’They’re afraid of it?’","No. That wasn’t quite right.","’They’re worshipping it.’","The enormous creature slowly raised its head. Its single red eye moved across the forest.","Then its mouth opened. The flesh around its jaw stretched impossibly wide.","Far wider than any normal anatomy should have allowed. Rows of irregular teeth emerged from folds of rotten flesh.","Noah’s eyes widened.","\"Oh, shi—\"","SKRRRRRREEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEECH!!!","The scream exploded across the forest. Noah immediately covered his ears.","\"ARGHHH!!\"","Pain stabbed through his skull. The air itself seemed to tremble. Nearby trees violently shook before several trunks cracked from the force.","The surface of the river in the distance erupted into countless ripples. Even the storm clouds above seemed disturbed.","Noah gritted his teeth as blood slowly trickled from one ear.","He watched the abomination helplessly. What could he possibly do against something like that? He tightened his grip around his sword.","Then something moved below the creature.","A dark mass slowly emerged from the crimson portal.","At first, Noah couldn’t understand what he was looking at.","The mass was enormous, black as pitch, and covered in strange cracks. Crimson light leaked through those cracks, as though something was burning inside it.","Then the mass twisted.","Squelch.","Several enormous tentacles emerged from the portal. Dozens of them came out.","They were thick enough to crush buildings, their surfaces covered in slick, oily flesh. Crimson energy continuously seeped from them, and wherever that corrupted substance touched the environment, it immediately began to erode.","HISSSSSSS","Trees dissolved. The ground blackened. Rock crumbled. The corruption spread with every movement of those monstrous appendages.","Noah stared at the destruction unfolding around him.","\"At this rate...\"","His voice became quiet.","\"...everything will be destroyed.\"","His gaze shifted toward the sky.","Akari was still somewhere within the storm.","She hadn’t regained control. And now this abomination had appeared.","’What am I supposed to do?’","Noah genuinely wondered if he was going to die.","’After everything that happened...’","His mind flashed back to the wooden house.","Training with Akari. Eating together with her, their conversations. Her lap pillows.","Falling asleep beside her. Those peaceful months had almost made him forget how dangerous this world truly was.","’After enjoying all those months with Akari... is this really how I’m going to die?’","Noah gave a bitter smile.","\"Life really does suck in the most retarded way.\"","But complaining wouldn’t save him.","His eyes hardened.","’No.’","There was still one possibility.","’Akari.’","Even in her current state, she was still Akari. If she could regain even a little control...","’She might be able to fight that thing.’","Noah had to survive until then.","WHOOSH!!","A gigantic tentacle suddenly shot toward him.","Noah’s pupils contracted.","\"Shit!\"","He immediately dashed sideways.","BOOOOOOM!!","The tentacle smashed into the ground where he had been standing. The earth exploded. A wave of corrupted energy spread across the soil.","Noah didn’t wait. He reinforced his body with mana and covered himself with another layer of ice.","’I need to run faster.’","He sprinted through the forest.","BOOM!","Another tentacle slammed down ahead of him. Noah abruptly changed direction.","BOOM!","Another struck from his left. He jumped over it. Then another came from the right. He twisted his body midair and narrowly avoided it. The forest had become a battlefield of gigantic moving limbs.","Every impact destroyed another section of the forest. Noah’s breathing became increasingly ragged.","’They’re everywhere!’","A tentacle suddenly crashed down directly ahead.","Noah couldn’t stop. Instead, he stepped onto its enormous surface.","CRACK!","Ice immediately formed beneath his boots.","HISSSSS!","The ice began melting almost instantly.","\"Seriously?!\"","Noah poured more mana into his feet. A fresh layer of ice formed.","It melted. Another layer replaced it.","Then another. Noah ran along the tentacle, constantly creating ice beneath his feet to prevent his boots from touching the corrosive surface.","’I can’t stay here for long!’","The tentacle suddenly twisted.","Noah nearly lost his balance.","\"Whoa!\"","He dropped into a crouch and drove one hand against the icy surface to steady himself.","WHOOSH!","A shadow appeared above him.","Noah looked up. Another tentacle was descending from the sky.","\"You’re kidding me!\"","There was nowhere to dodge. Noah tightened his grip around his sword. Mana surged through his core. A pale-blue aura condensed around the blade.","He swung upward with all his strength.","SHIIIIING!!","A huge, semi-transparent crescent of compressed frost erupted from the sword. The freezing arc was several meters wide, its curved edge shimmering with concentrated mana.","It shot upward.","SLAAAAASH!!","The enormous tentacle was cleanly split in two. The severed halves twisted violently before crashing into the forest.","BOOOOM!!","Corrupted fluid splattered across the ground, immediately eating through trees and soil.","Noah landed on the remaining tentacle, ice forming beneath his boots once again. He stared at the destruction around him.","His face became grim. \"There’s no end to them...\"","He looked toward the enormous abomination in the distance. The creature remained standing. Its single red eye slowly scanned the battlefield.","More tentacles continued emerging from the portal. And above it all, the storm surrounding Akari continued to rage.","Noah gritted his teeth.","’I can’t keep running forever.’","He raised his sword.","’I need to find a way to survive until Akari comes back to her senses.’","He exhaled slowly. This time, the ice surrounding his body began to change.","It spread across him, forming a complete suit of armor that covered his entire body. Then the ice climbed over his head, forming a helmet that enclosed his face. Noah was completely encased in ice armor.","’Alright...’","He calm down his emotions. There were only two things Noah could do right now. One, run, run and run, then survive somehow and wait for Akari... or damn just go, fight and get killed.","He looked behind him, toward the sky where the dragon was hidden among the clouds.","Then he looked forward.","Tentacles were coming straight toward him.","THUD!!","At the same time, the abomination, which had remained motionless for so long, finally moved.","It planted one hand against the ground. Since the portal was flat and horizontal, it used its arm to push itself upward.","Then its legs emerged from the portal.","They were enormous.","Its first leg slammed onto the ground.","BOOOOM!","A moment later, its second leg followed as the creature finally pulled its entire body out of the hole.","It rose to its full height seventy meters. Perhaps even eighty. The colossal abomination towered over the forest like a living mountain.","Noah smiled. He gathered strength in his legs and dashed forward. Enough running away."]},{"number":288,"title":"Chapter 288: NO CHANCE","paragraphs":["Crack!","Noah launched himself forward.","The ground beneath his foot fractured from the force of his push, forming a web of cracks across the muddy earth.","His sword gleamed with a sharp, pale-blue frost.","Ba-dump! Ba-dump!","His heartbeat thundered faster than ever.","Above him, the heavens continued their violent clash. Dark clouds spiraled across the sky as blue lightning tore through them, followed by deafening peals of thunder. Heavy rain poured down relentlessly, carried sideways by powerful winds.","Yet Noah didn’t slow down. His eyes were fixed ahead. The enormous abomination suddenly raised its head.","Its single crimson eye turned toward the sky toward Akari.","SKRRRRRREEEEEEEEEEEEEECH!!!","The creature released another shrill scream. The sound tore through the forest.","Noah’s head throbbed violently from that sound.","\"Ugh!\"","Pain stabbed through his skull, but he gritted his teeth and continued running.","’I can’t stop!’","Several tentacles suddenly shot toward him.","WHOOSH!","Noah twisted his body sideways. One passed inches from his shoulder. Another swept across his path.","He jumped. A third came from above. Noah ducked beneath it before leaping onto another tentacle. The moment his boots touched its surface.","HISSSSSS!","The ice beneath his feet began melting. Noah immediately poured more mana into his legs. Fresh frost formed beneath each step.","He ran faster and faster. His figure became nothing more than a blurred streak of pale-blue light moving through the rain.","SHING!","A tentacle struck toward him.","Noah swung his sword.","SLASH!","The freezing blade severed it cleanly, then another came.","SLASH!","Another fell. His movements became increasingly decisive. There was no hesitation anymore.","No fear, only determination.","’I have no choice.’","Noah suddenly leaped into the air. His eyes glowed with intense azure light. Mana surged violently from his core.","BOOOOM!","A gigantic four-meter-long sword materialized beneath him. Unlike his previous creations, this one was considerably thicker and wider. Noah landed on its frozen surface.","’Go!’","The massive ice sword shot forward.","WHOOSH!!!","It tore through the rain like an arrow. Noah crouched low, maintaining his balance while pouring an enormous amount of mana into the construct.","His temples throbbed. His mind strained under the concentration required to control such a massive weapon while simultaneously moving at high speed.","’This time... I can’t hold back.’","He had already defeated an abomination larger than thirty meters during his labyrinth expedition. And since then, he had grown considerably stronger. His core had advanced. His physical abilities had improved.","His swordsmanship had improved. His control over ice had improved. But this creature it was on another level entirely. And Noah knew that.","’If Akari fights this thing while she’s still out of control, the surrounding area will be destroyed.’","And Noah wouldn’t survive the aftermath. Waiting wasn’t an option. Running wasn’t an option.","’Then I’ll strike first.’","The abomination suddenly moved. Its enormous foot lifted from the ground and began stepping toward the direction of the raging dragon.","Noah’s expression hardened.","\"Not happening.\"","He released the restraints on his mana.","BOOOOOOM!!!","His entire core erupted. Mana flooded through his body.","WHOOSH! WHOOSH! WHOOSH!","One enormous ice sword materialized. Then another and another. Within seconds, more than twenty gigantic swords appeared throughout the storm. Each one was over twenty meters long.","They floated around the abomination like enormous pillars of frost, their edges gleaming beneath the lightning-filled sky.","The creature finally noticed him. Its gigantic crimson eye slowly turned toward the tiny human hovering in the distance.","For the first time it acknowledged Noah’s existence. Noah gripped his sword tightly.","\"Yeah.\"","His breathing was heavy. \"But I’m not going to let you reach her.\"","The abomination opened its enormous mouth.","SKRRRRR","Noah’s eyes widened.","’Here it comes.’","A torrent of crimson smoke suddenly erupted from its mouth.","FWOOSH!!!","The smoke spread through the air like a poisonous wave.","Noah immediately understood.","’That thing will eat through my ice armor.’","He didn’t hesitate.","\"Up!\"","He commanded the massive sword beneath his feet. The ice blade shot vertically upward like a rocket.","WHOOSH!!!","The crimson cloud passed beneath him. The moment it touched the surrounding trees.","HISSSSSSS—!!","Their surfaces blackened and began to dissolve.","Noah’s expression became grim.","’One touch and my defenses are gone.’","He looked down at the abomination. Then at the twenty massive swords surrounding it. A determined smile slowly formed on his face.","\"Alright...\"","He raised his sword. \"Let’s see how much you can take.\"","The twenty enormous swords remained suspended around the abomination. For a brief moment, everything seemed strangely still. Then Noah raised his hand and waved it down.","BOOOOOOM!!!","Every sword moved at once. They shot toward the abomination from every direction with terrifying speed, tearing through the rain and leaving trails of pale-blue frost behind them.","Noah’s eyes widened as he poured even more mana into their movements. His temples throbbed violently.","’Too many...’","He had never attempted to control this many massive constructs simultaneously. Each sword required a tremendous amount of concentration. And now he was controlling more than twenty of them at once.","His vision blurred for a moment. Blood trickled from his nose. But he didn’t stop.","\"Move!\"","The swords accelerated.","SHRAAAAAK!!!","The first massive blade slammed into the abomination’s shoulder. Another pierced through its chest. Two more crashed into its abdomen from opposite directions.","Several struck its arms and legs. One enormous sword drove straight through the side of its torso.","BOOOOOOM!!!","The combined impact shook the forest. The abomination’s gigantic body staggered.","SKRRRRRREEEEEEEEEEEEEECH!!!","It screamed. The sound shook the clouds.","First time, genuine pain appeared in its monstrous voice.","Noah’s eyes widened.","’It worked!’","But the swords hadn’t penetrated as deeply as he had hoped. The creature’s flesh seemed to resist them. The blades sank several meters into its body before losing momentum.","CRACK.","One sword began to fracture, then another.","Noah’s expression changed.","\"No...\"","CRACK! CRACK! CRACK!","The enormous ice swords shattered one after another. Thousands of fragments of frost scattered through the air. The abomination slowly straightened itself.","Noah stared.","The enormous wounds across its body began moving. The flesh around each injury twisted and crawled toward the center.","Squelch.","The holes closed. The torn flesh reconnected. The damaged muscles regenerated. Within seconds, the wounds had completely disappeared. It was as though Noah’s attack had never happened.","His pupils contracted.","\"It healed...?\"","No. That wasn’t healing. It was something far worse.","’It regenerated almost instantly.’","The abomination’s single eye locked onto him.","Noah felt his stomach drop.","\"Shit.\"","The creature raised one arm.","WHOOSH!!!","A gigantic tentacle shot toward him. Noah immediately commanded the sword beneath his feet to dive. The tentacle passed overhead.","BOOM!!!","Another followed.","Noah twisted sideways. A third struck him from behind.","CRACK!","His ice armor shattered. The impact sent him flying.","\"ARGH!\"","He spun through the air before crashing through several tree branches.","BOOM! BOOM!","His body finally slammed into the ground. Pain exploded through his back. Noah couldn’t breathe for a while.","\"Kh...\"","He coughed violently. Blood escaped from the corner of his mouth. His vision swayed.","’That one hit...’","He slowly pushed himself up. His ribs felt like they had been crushed. But there was no time to recover.","WHOOSH!","Another tentacle descended. Noah rolled away.","BOOM!!!","The ground exploded beside him. Mud and debris covered his body. He immediately created several ice pillars beneath himself.","SHING! SHING! SHING!","The spikes launched him into the air. He narrowly escaped another strike.","\"Come on!\"","His eyes glowed azure. A dozen ice spears materialized around him. He thrust his hand forward.","WHOOSH! WHOOSH! WHOOSH!","The spears shot toward the creature. The abomination raised one arm. Its flesh bulged. Then dozens of smaller appendages erupted from its arm.","CLANG! CLANG! CLANG!","The spears were intercepted. Some shattered. Others were swallowed by the creature’s flesh.","Noah’s expression became increasingly grim.","’Its defense is ridiculous.’","He clenched his teeth.","’Then I’ll attack from another direction.’","He created an ice platform beneath himself and launched forward. His sword became coated in a razor-thin layer of compressed frost.","SHING!","Noah descended toward the creature’s shoulder.","[Frozen Lotus—]","Before he could complete the technique.","WHOOSH!","A tentacle struck him from the side. Noah barely managed to raise his sword.","BOOM!!!","His body was sent flying. His arm went numb. He crashed into the ground and rolled several times before finally stopping. His breathing became ragged.","Blood ran down his forehead.","His left shoulder hung unnaturally. There his skin was decomposed on shoulder.","\"Fuck...\"","He forced himself upright. The abomination was still standing. Untouched, its single eye stared down at him.","Noah laughed weakly.","\"You’re really one annoying bastard...\"","Noah’s expression hardened.","’I can’t beat it like this. There’s fucking now chance. Not a single attack working on it.\"’","He looked toward the sky.","Lightning continued to surround Akari.","The storm was becoming more violent by the second.","His gaze returned to the abomination. Noah tightened his grip around his sword despite his trembling hands. He forced mana into his damaged body.","Pain surged through him.","He ignored it.","\"Come on...\"","Just the creature stared at Noah and the opened it’s mouth. \"HUMAN... STAY OUT OF MY WAY!!!\"","It’s loud horrifying voice spread though the forest. Noah stopped and looked at the creature with shock."]},{"number":289,"title":"Chapter 289: Lightning-Storm Dragon [1]","paragraphs":["The abomination suddenly stopped. Its enormous body remained motionless for several seconds. Then, for the first time, it spoke.","The voice was deep and distorted, as though several different voices were speaking through the same throat.","\"YOU...\"","Its enormous head slowly turned to the side. Then it stopped. That single crimson eye shifted back toward Noah.","\"YOU ARE THE SAME HUMAN WHO WAS WITH HIM...THE CHILD BLESS BY SUN\"","Noah froze. His pupils contracted. A chill ran through his entire body.","’He... he’s the same one.’","Noah remembered. That night in the dungeon. He and Damien had fought that grotesque creature with pale, oily skin. The monster hadn’t been acting on its own.","Something else had spoken through its body. Something that knew about Damien. Something that had called him the one blessed by the Sun God.","Noah had never forgotten that voice. And now it was standing before him.","’This thing is involved in all of this.’","His thoughts raced. ’It wants to kill Akari. But why?’","He wondered. Was it because she had completely awakened her dragon bloodline?","’Does her awakening pose some kind of threat to it?’","There were still too many questions. The dragon who had trapped Akari here couldn’t have been this creature. Akari had been imprisoned in this isolated region for decades.","The dragon had deliberately created the labyrinth. It had built the circular platform. It had carved the strange runes. And somehow, those runes had reacted when Akari finally awakened her bloodline completely.","That reaction had opened the portal.","’So the dragon created the conditions for this creature to appear. But why?’","Noah couldn’t understand. Then another thought struck him. His eyes widened.","’Damien.’","Damien had been the one who was supposed to come here. If everything had gone according to whatever plan existed. Damien would have entered this place.","He would have encountered Akari. And now he would have been standing here instead of Noah.","’Was this creature supposed to fight Damien?’","Noah’s expression became grim.","’And did that dragon deliberately arrange everything so Akari and Damien would eventually face this thing together?’","The possibility sent another chill through him. But before Noah could think any further.","\"DON’T THINK SO DEEPLY ABOUT THIS, HUMAN.\"","The abomination’s voice dragged him back to reality. Its enormous foot moved.","THUD!!!","The ground shook beneath Noah’s feet. It took another step.","THUD!!!","Dust and mud jumped from the earth. The creature lowered its head slightly.","\"I REMEMBER YOU.\"","Its enormous hand slowly rose.","\"YOU WERE THE ONE WHO DELIVERED THE FINAL BLOW TO MY PUPPET.\"","Noah’s face paled.","\"Shit...\"","The creature’s palm opened.","Squelch.","Dozens of tentacles erupted from its arm. They twisted through the air like living serpents.","Noah’s eyes widened. More than thirty of them shot toward him simultaneously.","They came from above, from the sides, from behind. There was nowhere to run.","’Too many!’","Noah forced his remaining mana into his body.","BOOM!","Multiple thick walls of ice erupted around him, one after another.","CRACK!","The first wall shattered.","BOOM!","The second was pierced by it and dissolved.","CRACK! CRACK!","The remaining barriers collapsed almost instantly.","Noah gritted his teeth.","’I can’t dodge all of them!’","The tentacles closed in. They were close to kill him, or rather erode him.","CRACKLE!!!","A blue flash suddenly tore through the stormy sky.","Noah’s eyes widened.","SHKKK!!!","A streak of blue lightning appeared directly before him, then another and another. Multiple lightning-colored trajectories flashed through the air so quickly that Noah could barely follow them.","The approaching tentacles were suddenly sliced apart.","SLASH! SLASH! SLASH!","Chunks of corrupted flesh fell around Noah. The severed tentacles writhed briefly before dissolving into the mud.","Noah stood frozen. He couldn’t even see who had attacked. All he could hear was the continuous crackling of lightning.","Something was moving. Something impossibly fast. More blue streaks flashed across the battlefield.","Every tentacle that approached Noah was cut apart before reaching him. Then the lightning reached the abomination’s arm.","SHKKKK!!!","A blue slash passed through its enormous limb. The massive arm was severed as cleanly as if it had been made of butter.","BOOOOM!!!","The arm crashed into the ground. The abomination roared.","\"ARGHHHHH!!!\"","Its enormous eye turned toward the sky.","\"YOU FINALLY CAME!\"","The creature’s voice shook with fury.","\"STORM DRAGON!!!\"","Noah’s eyes widened.","’Storm Dragon...’","A powerful pressure suddenly descended upon the battlefield. The rain itself seemed to bend around something. A blue silhouette hovered in the storm-filled sky.","A woman. She wore a deep-blue kimono, though the transformation had torn through the fabric around her back.","Two enormous dark-sapphire wings extended from her shoulders. They looked almost like crystalline wings beneath the flashes of lightning. But they were made by her dragon transformation.","Two dark horns with a faint blue sheen curved from her head. Her eyes glowed with an intense azure light. Vertical pupils stared down coldly at the abomination below.","Her presence alone made the surrounding air tremble. She was taller than Noah remembered—nearly 188 centimeters in her current awakened form or maybe more.","In her right hand was a katana. Blue lightning crawled continuously along its blade.","Crackle... crackle...","The woman slowly descended through the rain. Her expression was completely different from the gentle Akari Noah knew.","There was no warmth, no smile, no softness. He face was full of cold, terrifying composure.","Noah stared at her for several seconds. Then he swallowed.","\"...Akari.\"","She didn’t look at him. Her entire attention remained fixed on the abomination. The creature’s severed arm was already beginning to regenerate.","Flesh crawled over the wound. The abomination snarled.","\"YOU...\"","Akari raised her katana. Blue lightning intensified around the blade.","BOOOOOOM!!!","A thunderclap erupted overhead.","Noah immediately understood something. This was no longer a fight he could participate in. The pressure radiating from both beings was overwhelming.","Even standing nearby made his body tremble. He slowly stepped backward.","Then another step.","’Nope. Absolutely not.’","He turned around.","\"I’ve done enough. I tried enough.\"","His body was already covered in wounds. His mana was dangerously low. His shoulder had decomposed flesh.","And these two monsters.","No, these two beings were far beyond anything he could currently handle. Even standing close to them was sucide.","Noah started running.","’This isn’t a battle between mortals anymore.’","BOOOOOOM!!!","Lightning and corrupted energy collided. The forest shook violently.","Noah didn’t look back.","’If I stay anywhere near them, I’ll die from the shockwaves before I even get a chance to run.’","He poured whatever mana remained into his legs. He glanced over his shoulder for one brief moment.","She stood alone before the enormous abomination, lightning surrounding her like a living storm.","\"I’m going to leave the monster to you.\"","---","Akari moved.","BOOOOM!!!","A streak of blue lightning exploded through the rain.","She disappeared from her position and reappeared directly in front of the abomination, moving so quickly that one couldn’t even follow her movement with normal eyes.","Her katana flashed.","SHIIING!!!","A razor-thin arc of blue lightning sliced across the creature’s enormous torso. The abomination’s flesh split open.","SQUELCH!","Dark, corrupted blood sprayed outward as a deep wound appeared across its body. The creature staggered backward.","\"GRRRRAAAAAHHH!!!\"","Akari didn’t give it a chance to recover, another flash.","BOOM!","She appeared at its side, another slash.","SHRAAAK!!!","The creature’s thick arm was cut open from shoulder to elbow. Akari vanished again.","CRACKLE!!!","A flash of blue lightning appeared behind the abomination. Her katana struck downward.","BOOOOM!!!","The impact drove the creature several meters into the ground.","Noah stopped running and stared for a moment before shaking his head.","’She’s way too fast.’","Then he continued running. The battlefield behind him had already become a disaster. Dark clouds covered the sky, while blue lightning continuously gathered around Akari.","KRA-KOOOOOM!!!","Lightning suddenly rained from the heavens. One bolt struck a cluster of smaller monsters crawling out of the crimson portal.","BOOM!!!","They were instantly incinerated. Another bolt descended.","BOOOOM!!!","A second group vanished in a burst of blue-white lightning.","Noah kept running.","’She’s controlling the lightning...’","He glanced upward. Another bolt appeared directly above him. His heart jumped.","\"Wait—\"","The lightning suddenly changed direction.","CRACK!!!","It struck a monster several meters behind him instead. The creature had been preparing to pounce on Noah, but the lightning vaporized it before it could move.","Noah blinked.","\"...She deliberately avoided me?\"","He looked toward the sky. Akari was already fighting the abomination again. She didn’t look in his direction.","Yet every lightning strike that descended near Noah seemed to avoid him by a deliberate margin. Another monster rushed from the trees.","ROAR!!!","Noah raised his sword. But before he could attack.","KRA-BOOOOM!!!","A bolt struck directly between them. The monster disappeared in an instant.","Noah’s hair stood on end from the static. He stared at the smoking ground.","\"...Okay.\"","A small smile appeared on his exhausted face. ’She’s protecting me.’","That realization gave him a strange sense of relief. But the situation remained catastrophic. The lightning strikes were becoming more frequent.","BOOM!","Others struck the ground several meters away.","CRACK!","Trees caught fire despite the rain. The flames spread rapidly through the dry branches and undergrowth, feeding on the chaos created by the battle.","---","[A/N: I feel bad for letting Noah face such dangerous entity, and also feel like that I show that abomination weak. Alright time to make it more strong!!!!]"]},{"number":290,"title":"Chapter 290: Lightning-Storm Dragon [2]","paragraphs":["Akari moved through the storm like a streak of blue lightning.","Every time she disappeared, a flash of light followed. She reappeared somewhere else a moment later, her katana cutting through the abomination’s corrupted flesh before she vanished again.","Yet despite her overwhelming speed, her expression remained tense.","’What is this thing?’","She narrowly avoided one of its enormous tentacles. The corrupted flesh brushed against the edge of her kimono.","Hissss!","The fabric instantly began to dissolve.","Akari’s eyes narrowed. Even a brief touch is enough to decompose matter.","She looked at her katana.","The blade was still glowing with blue lightning, but small portions of its surface had already begun to deteriorate whenever it came into contact with the creature’s body.","’My sword won’t last much longer either.’","She clicked her tongue. This was a serious problem. She could feel it clearly now.","The creature wasn’t simply powerful. Its very existence was dangerous. Even her own raw destructive powers might not be able to kill it.","Even approaching it made the instincts she had gained from her awakened bloodline scream at her to be cautious.","And Noah, her thoughts briefly shifted toward the young man who had been fighting this thing alone.","’What you did was incredibly foolish.’","A faint smile almost appeared on her lips.","’But... it actually helped me.’","Akari remembered what had happened after she completely awakened her bloodline.","The moment the final restraint broke, an overwhelming amount of power had flooded through her body.","It wasn’t simply an increase in strength. It was as if something ancient had awakened alongside her bloodline.","Her senses had become sharper. Her body had transformed. Her connection to lightning and storms had reached a completely different level.","But she hadn’t been prepared for the sheer intensity of it.","Her consciousness had been swallowed by the storm.","At first, she had tried to resist. Then her thoughts had become fragmented. Her emotions disappeared one by one.","And eventually, she felt as though she were no longer controlling her own body.","It was like being trapped inside her own mind.","Countless invisible chains seemed to bind her consciousness, preventing her from taking control.","She could still perceive what was happening around her.","She could see. She could hear. She could feel. But she couldn’t stop herself. Her body moved according to another instinct.","A primitive instinct. That was storm and thunder and destruction. She wanted to summon lightning.","She wanted to fill the sky with clouds. She wanted to create storms and let thunder shake the entire world.","There was no reason behind those desires.","There was no hatred nor purpose.","Just an overwhelming urge to release the power inside her.","Is this what it means to become a true dragon?","The thought had terrified her.","Because if she surrendered completely to that instinct, she wouldn’t be Akari anymore.","She would simply become a powerful beast driven by its bloodline.","And then she remembered Noah.His presence. His voice. His stubbornness. His ridiculous behavior. His constant teasing. His laughter. He was now the closest person to her. Very important.","And then she heard him calling her name.","\"AKARI!\"","His voice had pierced through the chaos. At first, it had been nothing more than a distant sound.","Then it came again.","\"IT’S ME, NOAH!\"","His voice came again and again. He kept calling for her despite knowing how dangerous she was.","Even when she attacked him, he refused to stop. His voice gradually became clearer. It reached somewhere deep within her consciousness.","And then she realized something. Noah was in danger. Because of her. The thought terrified her more than losing control itself.","’I might kill him.’","That realization became the first crack in the chains surrounding her consciousness.","She remembered why she had been fighting against her bloodline for so many years.","She didn’t want to lose herself. She didn’t want to become a monster. And she certainly didn’t want to hurt someone she cared about so much.","Noah’s voice gave her something to hold onto. Slowly, she began pulling against those invisible chains.","It wasn’t easy. The storm inside her fought back.","Her body wanted to continue destroying everything around her.","But she kept resisting. One chain broke then another. Little by little, her consciousness returned to the surface.","Until finally she opened her eyes. Not the eyes of a mindless dragon.","Her own as she regained control of her body. The storm was still raging inside her. The immense power was still there.","But now she was the one controlling it. That was the final step of her awakening. Not merely gaining the power of her bloodline.","But possessing the strength of will to control it. Akari’s eyes narrowed as she returned to the present.","The abomination attacked again. She vanished in a flash of blue lightning.","SHING!!!","Her katana sliced through another portion of its corrupted body.","She reappeared several meters away, lightning crackling around her wings.","’I finally awakened completely. I am no longer a human... but a dragon.’","Her gaze hardened.","’And I won’t let anyone take that control away from me.’","She looked toward the direction Noah had escaped.","A faint softness appeared in her eyes thinking of Noah.","Then her expression turned cold again.","She faced the abomination.","\"Now...\"","Lightning gathered around her.","\"...it’s my turn.\"","Blue lightning crackled violently across Akari’s body, wrapping around her like a living current.","The same azure energy crawled along the length of her katana, causing the blade to glow brightly enough to illuminate the storm-darkened sky.","The wind responded to her presence. Clouds churned overhead.","Thunder rolled across the heavens. For a moment, the entire forest seemed to exist beneath her command.","The abomination stared at her. Then its enormous mouth slowly curved into a grotesque grin.","\"REMINDS ME OF THE OLD STORM DRAGON...\"","Its single crimson eye narrowed.","\"...BUT HE WAS FAR STRONGER.\"","Akari’s expression immediately changed.","’Old Storm Dragon?’ Her grip tightened around her katana.","’Is this creature connected to the previous Storm Dragon?’","There was no time to think about it. The abomination’s body suddenly expanded.","SQUELCH!","More than fifty enormous tentacles erupted from its back and shoulders. They twisted through the air before shooting toward Akari from every direction.","Akari looked at them calmly. She lowered her katana.","Then she swung it. Not toward the creature. Simply through the air. As if she was commanding something.","WHOOM!!!","The wind changed direction instantly. Every gust surrounding the battlefield suddenly converged toward the abomination. The air began spinning.","It spun faster and faster.","BOOOOOOM!!!","A gigantic tornado erupted around the creature. Its massive body disappeared inside the violent vortex.","The fifty tentacles were dragged upward, twisting helplessly inside the rotating winds. The abomination roared.","\"GRRRAAAAAAAHHH!!!\"","Akari raised her katana toward the sky. Lightning gathered between the clouds. Thousands of blue sparks danced across the heavens.","Her eyes flashed.","\"Fall.\"","KRA-KOOOOOM!!!","A massive bolt of lightning descended from the clouds.","It struck the tornado. From different parts of clouds, they came down and covered at tornado.","BOOM!","BOOM!","BOOM!","Lightning continuously poured into the vortex. The entire tornado turned brilliant blue.","The forest was illuminated as brightly as daylight. The abomination’s silhouette could be seen twisting inside the storm.","Its corrupted flesh burned wherever the lightning touched it.","Yet it didn’t fall. Instead, the creature planted its enormous feet into the ground.","THUD!","The earth cracked beneath it. Its remaining tentacles stabbed into the ground like anchors. The tornado began slowing.","Akari’s eyes narrowed.","’It’s resisting the storm?’","The creature suddenly pulled its arms apart.","BOOOOM!!!","A violent shockwave exploded outward. The tornado ruptured.","Wind tore through the forest, flattening trees and throwing debris in every direction.","Akari crossed her katana before her body. The gale slammed into her.","Her wings spread wide. She remained suspended in the air.","The abomination emerged from the dissipating vortex. Large portions of its body were charred and smoking.","But the wounds were already closing. Flesh crawled over the damaged areas.","Akari’s gaze became colder.","\"Regeneration?\"","She raised her katana. Blue lightning condensed around the blade until it became almost solid.","The creature opened its mouth.","\"YOU HAVE THE SAME EYES.\"","Akari paused.","\"THE SAME STORM.\"","Its grin widened.","\"BUT YOU ARE NOT HIM.\"","Akari’s eyes narrowed.","\"Who are you? Who is this storm dragon you are talking about?\"","The creature didn’t answer. Instead, its enormous body suddenly lunged forward.","BOOOOOOM!!!","The ground exploded beneath its feet.","Akari disappeared. The creature’s fist smashed through empty air.","Before it could react.","SHING!","A blue flash appeared behind its neck. Akari’s katana swept across. A deep cut opened. The creature roared and swung its arm backward.","Akari vanished again. She reappeared above its head. Lightning gathered around her wings. Then she descended.","BOOOOOOM!!!","Her katana struck the creature’s shoulder with the force of a thunderbolt.","The impact drove it down onto one knee. The forest shook violently. Akari landed several meters away. Shockwave shot from their battle shook the whole dimension.","Her breathing remained steady. But her eyes were focused. It’s powerful. She looked at the rapidly regenerating wound.","But it can be damaged. Lightning began gathering around her again.","The storm answered. And this time, Akari didn’t intend to give the creature even a moment to recover."]},{"number":291,"title":"Chapter 291: Lightning-Storm Dragon [3]","paragraphs":["Noah had retreated more than four kilometers from the battlefield. Yet even at that distance, he could still feel the shockwaves rolling through the forest.","BOOOOOOM!!!","The ground trembled beneath his feet. Noah turned around. His eyes widened.","The battle in the distance looked less like a fight and more like a natural disaster given form.","Akari streaked across the storm clouds like a miniature blue star, her entire body wrapped in lightning. Every movement left behind a brilliant trail of azure light.","Then the sky erupted.","BOOOOOOM!!!","Hundreds of lightning bolts descended simultaneously. They converged upon the abomination, turning the entire battlefield into a sea of blue-white destruction.","Trees were torn apart. The ground split. Fire spread wildly through the forest despite the relentless rain, fed by the continuous lightning strikes that ignited everything they touched.","Noah swallowed. But what truly frightened him wasn’t Akari.","It was the creature.","\"...It’s growing.\"","His expression became grim. The abomination’s body had become noticeably larger than before.","’How is that possible?’","---","Meanwhile Akari continued her assault.She moved through the battlefield with terrifying precision.","Her katana swept horizontally. A gigantic web of lightning-infused slashes spread across the abomination’s torso.","The creature’s flesh tore apart. Before the pieces could even fall. Akari vanished. She reappeared above its head.","Her wings spread wide. The storm clouds twisted around her. She raised her katana vertically. For one brief moment, everything became silent.","Then she brought the blade down.","KRAAAAAAAAAA-BOOOOOOM!!!","A colossal crescent of blue lightning descended from the heavens. It struck the abomination from head to waist.","The force was so tremendous that the earth beneath it split open. For kilometers length.","The slash continued beyond the creature. A distant mountain caught the edge of the attack.","BOOOOOOM!!!","Its peak was cleaved apart. The abomination was split cleanly into two enormous halves. Akari didn’t even pause.","She disappeared. A flash of blue crossed the battlefield.","SHING!","Another slash.","SHING!","Another.","SHING!","Another.","Her movements became impossible to follow. She cut through its arms.","Its torso. Its shoulders. Its legs.Every strike carried enough force to tear apart enormous sections of the landscape.","The abomination’s body was shredded into countless pieces. Yet Akari’s expression remained cold.","’It’s still alive.’","The scattered flesh began moving. Chunks of black-red meat crawled toward one another.","They merged. Bones twisted. Flesh knitted together. Within seconds, the abomination began reforming.","Akari’s eyes narrowed.","’So even that isn’t enough.’","Lightning gathered around her. She raised one hand. The entire sky answered.","KRAK!","Lightning struck the battlefield, again and again. A continuous storm descended upon the abomination.","Its body was burned, torn apart, and reduced to charred pieces. Yet it continued regenerating. The creature’s flesh was already so corrupted that ordinary wounds seemed meaningless.","Lightning hurt it. Akari could tell that much.","It screamed whenever her attacks struck.","But the damage never lasted.","And worst it was becoming larger. Every time it regenerated, its body seemed slightly more massive than before.","Akari floated above the battlefield, rain streaming down her face.","Her blue eyes remained fixed on the creature.","’What are you?’","The abomination slowly stood again. Its body had become even larger than before.","Its single crimson eye stared at her. Then it smiled.","Akari tightened her grip. The storm around her intensified. She understood something.","’I can’t simply overpower it.’","The creature wasn’t fighting like a normal opponent. It was enduring, adapting and frowing. And somehow, the longer the battle continued, the more dangerous it became.","Akari’s gaze shifted briefly toward the distant forest, toward Noah.","’Please... keep running.’","She couldn’t afford to hold back anymore.","Her wings spread. The clouds above began rotating into an enormous vortex. Lightning gathered inside them until the entire sky became blue.","Akari raised her katana.","\"Then I’ll destroy you before you have the chance to grow any further.\"","The abomination answered with a deafening roar.","GWRRRAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA!!!","The two beings launched themselves forward simultaneously. One was a Storm Dragon wielding the fury of heaven.","The other was an abomination born from corruption and countless fused creatures.","Their collision created a shockwave that swept across kilometers of forest.","BOOOOOOOOOOOOOOM!!!","For several seconds, there was no distinction between sky and earth. Only lightning, darkness and fire.","And the thunderous clash of two beings whose battle had already surpassed anything humans could comprehend.","The battle showed no signs of ending.","Akari hovered above the devastated forest, lightning continuously crawling across her body. Her kimono was torn in several places, and her breathing had become heavier.","Yet her eyes remained sharp.","Below her, the abomination continued to regenerate. Its enormous body was already larger than before.","’Why it’s not stopping... is it somehow sucking life from everything and getting bigger again? Or corrupting his surrounding makes him stronger?’","Akari clenched her teeth. She couldn’t allow this battle to continue indefinitely. Her gaze shifted toward the sky.","The storm clouds responded immediately.","They began rotating faster and faster. Until an enormous vortex formed above the battlefield.","Countless strands of blue lightning gathered within it. Akari raised her katana.","’Let’s try this.’","The lightning suddenly condensed. From within the storm, an enormous dragon-shaped mass emerged.","Its body was entirely composed of blue lightning. It had a long serpentine body, enormous wings, and a head crowned with blazing horns.","The Lightning Dragon opened its mouth.","[Raiko Ryujin]","ROOOOOOAR!!!","Thunder exploded across the heavens.","Akari gripped her katana with both hands.","Then she pulled it downward.","The Lightning Dragon followed. It plunged from the heavens like a divine beast descending upon the earth.","The abomination looked upward.","Its enormous eye widened.","THUNDER-BOOOOOOOOOOM!!!","The dragon crashed into the battlefield.","An explosion of blue lightning erupted across several kilometers. It there were a city, by now it would have been destroyed by her attacks.","Trees were vaporized. The earth was torn apart. The shockwave swept through the surrounding forest, flattening everything in its path.","For several seconds, the entire battlefield disappeared beneath a blinding blue light.","Crack.","Akari froze. She looked down at her katana.","A thin fracture ran along the blade.","CRACK!","The blade shattered. Fragments of metal fell through the rain. Akari stared at the broken weapon.","The countless previous clashes had finally taken their toll. The abomination’s flesh had continuously corroded the blade every time they came into contact.","Her only weapon had reached its limit. She looked toward the explosion. The smoke slowly dispersed. The abomination was still there.","Its body was badly damaged. But it was regenerating.","And its enormous form had grown even larger. Akari’s expression darkened.","\"This is getting troublesome.\"","Then she sensed something. Her eyes shifted toward the distance. Even through the storm, her enhanced senses could perceive Noah.","Nearly four kilometers away.","’Still too close.’","A battle between them at this level could easily devastate everything within several kilometers.","Akari disappeared.","BOOM!","A streak of blue lightning crossed the forest.","In less than a few seconds, she reached Noah.","He barely had time to react.","\"Akari–\"","Akari grabbed him. Before he could finish speaking, the world became a blur.","BOOOOOOM!!!","She carried him through the forest at terrifying speed, crossing kilometer after kilometer.","Noah’s hair whipped violently in the wind.","\"Wait! Akari, what are—\"","She didn’t answer. She continued moving. She nearly went more than thirty kilometers.","Only then did she finally slow down.","She gently placed Noah on the ground in a relatively untouched section of forest.","Noah stumbled slightly before regaining his balance.","\"Akari, wait—\"","She looked at him. For a moment, their eyes met. Her expression was calm. But beneath that calmness, Noah could see determination.","\"Let me handle this.\"","Noah’s eyes widened.","\"Akari...\"","\"Stay here.\"","She turned away. Blue lightning began gathering around her body.","Noah instinctively stepped forward.","\"Akari!\"","She didn’t look back. A moment later.","BOOOOOOM!!!","She shot into the sky.","Noah could only watch her rapidly disappearing figure. Then the storm changed. The clouds above the battlefield began rotating violently.","A tremendous pressure spread across the sky.","Noah’s expression changed.","\"What...?\"","A brilliant blue light erupted from the distant storm. Akari’s figure disappeared completely within it. Her body began changing.","Lightning enveloped her from head to toe.","Her wings expanded. Her limbs transformed.","Her body grew larger and larger. Scales formed across her skin, each one shining with a deep sapphire-blue glow. Her horns lengthened.","Her claws emerged. Her tail extended behind her. Within moments, the human figure Noah knew was gone.","In her place was an enormous dragon.","Approximately seventy-five meters from head to tail, her massive wings stretched across the storm clouds.","Lightning crawled between her scales.","Thunder answered every movement of her wings.","She slowly raised her head.","The entire forest fell beneath her shadow.","Then Akari opened her enormous jaws.","ROOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOAAAAAAR!!!","Her roar shook the heavens. Lightning erupted throughout the clouds.","The storm itself seemed to bow before her.","Far away, Noah stared upward in complete silence.","\"She’s crazy!!\"","Another roar echoed across the sky.","And then the Storm Dragon charged back toward the abomination. This time, Akari was going taste her powers as true dragon."]},{"number":292,"title":"Chapter 292: Lightning-Storm Dragon [4]","paragraphs":["The Storm Dragon soared through the heavens. Her enormous wings beat once.","BOOOOOOM!!!","The resulting wind tore through the clouds, sending them spiraling across the sky. Akari no longer needed to consciously summon the storm.","It simply obeyed her. The wind bent around her body. Lightning crawled between her sapphire scales.","Thunder rolled wherever she flew. The entire sky had become an extension of her will. Below, the abomination moved.","THUD.","It took one step. The earth sank beneath its foot.","THUD.","Then it took another. Trees snapped around it. The corrupted flesh spreading from its body decomposed everything it touched.","Then the creature began running.","BOOOOOOM!!!","Each step shook the forest like an earthquake.","Dozens of enormous tentacles dragged across the ground, crushing trees and carving trenches through the earth.","Akari looked down. Her enormous eye narrowed. She opened her jaws.","A brilliant blue light began gathering inside her throat.","CRACKLE... CRACKLE...","Lightning accumulated, she conjured more and more. Until the light inside her mouth became almost blinding.","ROOOOOOOOOOOAAAAAR!!!","A gigantic beam of blue lightning erupted from her jaws. It shot across the sky like a divine judgment.","KRAAAAAAAAAA-BOOOOOOM!!!","The beam struck the abomination head-on. The impact swallowed its entire upper body.","The surrounding forest disappeared beneath the blue radiance.","Trees were vaporized. The earth exploded.","A massive trench was carved across the landscape as the beam continued forward.","The ground beneath the creature melted into glowing stone before being blasted apart completely.","For a while, the entire battlefield became nothing but blue light. Then a voice emerged from within the destruction.","\"HAHAHAHAHAHA!!!\"","The abomination’s laughter echoed through the storm.","\"THAT’S IT!\"","Its enormous silhouette remained inside the beam.","\"SHOW ME YOUR WHOLE POWER!\"","Akari’s pupils narrowed.","The beam intensified.","BOOOOOOOOOOM!!!","The explosion expanded outward. A shockwave tore through the forest for kilometers.","Yet the abomination remained standing. Its body had been blasted apart in several places. But the wounds were already closing.","Flesh crawled. Whatever bones reformed. The missing portions reconstructed themselves.","And when the beam finally disappeared. The creature was larger.","Akari’s expression hardened. It grew again. The abomination spread its arms.","Its flesh expanded outward like a living mass. Tentacles erupted from its torso.","Hundreds and then thousands. They spread across the surrounding forest, wrapping around trees and sinking into the ground.","The earth immediately began turning black. Red smoke poured from its body. The smoke climbed into the heavens, mixing with the storm clouds.","The beautiful blue sky slowly became crimson. The corruption spread faster.","Grass withered around them and trees rotted. Rocks cracked. Even the rain began evaporating whenever it touched the creature’s flesh.","Akari looked around. Her expression became colder. If this continues, the entire region will be destroyed. She spread her enormous wings.","The clouds above her began rotating. The storm became enormous. Lightning gathered across the entire horizon.","KRAK!","One bolt, then another, then hundreds. The sky became a web of blue lightning. Akari raised one claw. Every bolt suddenly converged toward a single point above her.","The energy condensed. The storm became unnaturally quiet. Then Akari brought her claw down.","FALL.","KRAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA-BOOOOOOM!!!","The heavens exploded. A colossal pillar of lightning descended. It was so enormous that it illuminated the landscape for dozens of kilometers.","The bolt struck the abomination. The impact created an explosion that swallowed everything around it.","The ground ruptured. A crater formed beneath the creature. The shockwave flattened the forest outward in every direction.","For kilometers, trees were uprooted and thrown through the air. The force was enough to devastate an area comparable to a small city.","Noah, watching from far away had started to run away once again.","\"What the hell...\"","The explosion continued expanding. Blue lightning raced across the ground like rivers. The earth cracked for hundreds of meters.","Mountains in the distance trembled.","Silence spread once again.","Akari remained suspended above the devastated landscape.","Her enormous chest rose and fell. She stared downward. Smoke covered the battlefield.","Did it finally.","THUD.","Something moved.","Akari’s eye widened. A gigantic hand emerged from the crater.","Then another, the abomination slowly pulled itself upright.","Its body was horribly damaged. Large portions had been completely destroyed. Yet its flesh began rebuilding itself.","Squelch.","Crack.","Squelch.","New flesh formed. Bones twisted into place. Tentacles grew from its back. Its enormous torso expanded.","And then it became even larger than before.","Akari’s expression darkened. The creature looked upward. Its single crimson eye glowed brighter.","\"MORE.\"","Its voice shook the air.","\"MORE!!!\"","Its arms spread wide.","\"YOUR LIGHTNING... YOUR STORM...\"","Its grin widened.","\"...COULD NEVER HARM ME!\"","Akari stared at it.","For the first time, she understood the horrifying nature of her opponent.","She could destroy it. But destruction alone wasn’t enough. Every time she damaged it, the creature regenerated.","Every time it regenerated, it seemed to become stronger. As if it was sucking energy from everything and becoming stronger.","And while Akari’s attacks were destroying the world around them, the abomination was consuming the destruction itself.","The crimson smoke thickened. The storm clouds began turning red.","Akari slowly lowered her head. Lightning crackled across her horns.","’Then I’ll have to find another way.’","She couldn’t feel helpless. Not after possessing strength enough to destroy cities, millions of people army in single attack.","But that power means nothing against her opponent. All her abilities, magic spells or anything looked so useless after fighting the abomination.","Using them won’t have any effect of monster. Never she had thought that after reaching pinnacle of human, after becoming dragon, she would still struggle.","The rain falling from the red sky now even have that creatures energy. It corrode even her lightly as it fell on her scales. But he defense was too strong. So they were bearable.","Her enormous wings spread. The sky darkened beneath them. She wasn’t retreating.","She wasn’t afraid. If anything, her gaze became even colder. The abomination roared.","Akari answered with a thunderous dragon’s roar of her own.","ROOOOOOOOOOOOOOOAAAAAAR!!!","One was the fury of the heavens. The other was the corruption of something that should never have existed.","The ground beneath the abomination suddenly bulged. Akari’s instincts screamed.","BOOOOOOM!!!","Dozens of enormous tentacles erupted from the earth at once. They shot toward her like black-red spears, tearing through the forest as they rose.","Akari immediately accelerated.","KRAK!!!","Blue lightning exploded behind her. Her enormous body became a streak of azure light as she flew upward.","The first wave of tentacles missed. Then another wave emerged.","They followed her relentlessly, twisting through the sky as if they could sense her movements.","Akari twisted her enormous body between them. One passed beneath her wing. Another narrowly missed her head.","She accelerated again.","The battlefield below was becoming a sea of corrupted flesh. Then the abomination moved.","THUD!","Its enormous foot slammed into the ground.","BOOOOOOM!!!","The earth collapsed beneath it. The creature crouched.","Then it jumped. The force of the movement created a gigantic crater where it had stood.","BOOOOOOM!!!","The abomination launched itself into the sky like a mountain thrown by an unseen force.","Akari’s eyes widened.","’It’s faster!’","Despite being lightning dragon, her speed in dragon form was not fast, mostly because of her weight and size.","Still it was not like she couldn’t run.","But the creature rapidly closed the distance. Its enormous hand reached toward her. Then its palm opened.","Hundreds of tentacles burst from it. They spread outward like a massive net.","Akari twisted sideways. Lightning exploded from her body. A wave of blue electricity swept through the tentacles.","The majority of them burned instantly. Charred pieces of corrupted flesh rained from the sky.","But there were too many. Several tentacles slipped through the lightning. One wrapped around Akari’s left leg. Another wrapped around her ankle.","Then another coiled around her lower leg.","Akari’s eyes narrowed.","She tried to pull away.","SNNNKKK!","The tentacles tightened. Their corrupted surface began reacting with her scales.","HISSSSSSS!","A thin layer of her sapphire scales started deteriorating.","The brilliant blue surface darkened. Small pieces began crumbling away. Akari felt a sharp pain travel through her leg, it was far too painful compared to any pain she every felt.","’Yes... it’s not only decomposing but also sucking energy from everything it touches!!’","She understood it.","Her expression changed. It’s penetrating my scales. She immediately flooded her leg with lightning.","---","[A/N: Sorry guys for less Chapter update for last few days. Kind of busy in real life. Sigh wanted to end this arc before end of this month. Hope I can do it. Even I feel like I am dragging it so will try to stop it and move faster from next Chapter.","And I probably have to visit my village after two days. For a function at relatives. Might get busy. Anyways, I will try to write extra Chapters for those days. So prolly no worry.","Also guys what do you think about a frost scythe as main weapon for Noah? I have been thinking about this for a while now.","Give your opinion in comment section.]"]},{"number":293,"title":"Chapter 293: Lightning-Storm Dragon [5]","paragraphs":["CRACKLE!","The tentacles recoiled beneath the surge of lightning.","But they didn’t let go. Instead, the abomination tightened its grip. Akari’s enormous body was suddenly dragged backward through the sky. His strength was far more strong than she had expected.","Her eyes narrowed. She had expected resistance, but not this. The creature’s single crimson eye remained fixed on her.","Its grotesque mouth slowly stretched open.","\"YOU CANNOT ESCAPE.\"","More tentacles erupted from its arm.","Akari’s wings spread violently.","BOOOOM!","The surrounding clouds exploded outward from the sheer force of her movement.","She pulled against the restraints with all her strength.","Lightning gathered around her trapped leg, growing brighter with every passing second.","Her eyes flashed.","\"Don’t underestimate me.\"","KRAAAAAAAAAAAK!!!","A tremendous surge of blue lightning erupted from her body.","The tentacles began burning.","One after another, their corrupted flesh blackened and crumbled.","The restraints loosened.","But before Akari could completely break free—","BOOOOOOOOOOOM!!!","The abomination’s other hand slammed into her.","Akari barely managed to raise her wings. The impact sent her enormous body flying through the clouds.","She spun several times before finally stabilizing herself. Her wings spread wide.","She stopped. Then slowly looked down at her leg. Several sapphire scales had been damaged.","Blood trickled between them.","Akari’s expression became colder.","’That thing can actually injure me...’","She raised her gaze.","The abomination remained suspended in the sky, surrounded by countless writhing tentacles.","Below it, the forest continued to rot. Akari’s claws slowly tightened. Blue lightning crawled across her body.","Then she raised both wings. The atmosphere suddenly changed. The storm clouds above began rotating.","A tremendous pressure descended over the battlefield.","RUMBLE...","A gigantic magic circle appeared high above the forest.","Then another and another.","Concentric rings of ancient lightning runes formed across the heavens, spreading farther and farther until they covered several kilometers of sky.","The entire battlefield was illuminated by brilliant azure light. Even the crimson clouds were pushed aside.","The abomination looked upward.","For the first time, its expression seemed slightly interested.","Akari hovered beneath the enormous formation.","Her mana surged violently. She poured an enormous amount of energy into the spell.","The surrounding air trembled. Lightning began gathering within the magic circle. Countless strands converged toward its center.","The brightness became almost unbearable. For one brief moment, the entire forest looked as though dawn had arrived.","Akari’s eyes glowed intensely.","[Celestial Thunderstrike]","There was silence everywhere.","KRAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAK!!!","The heavens split open. An enormous pillar of lightning descended from the magic circle. It was so massive that its width covered nearly an entire kilometer.","The bolt struck the abomination directly.","BOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOM!!!","The world disappeared beneath blue-white radiance. Lightning spread outward from the impact point like countless rivers of destruction.","The earth ruptured.","Trees were instantly vaporized.","The ground was blasted apart, forming an enormous crater that expanded across the battlefield.","A shockwave swept through the forest.","Dust and debris were thrown kilometers into the air.","Even the storm clouds were violently displaced.","Akari remained high above the battlefield, breathing heavily.","She watched and waiting.","The dust cloud slowly began to settle. Her eyes moved toward the center of the devastation.","Toward the circular platform. Over it was the crimson portal. The waist length pillars having red glowing crystals above it, from them two crystal were broken and not blinking anymore, only two of them.","Akari’s expression stiffened.","’What... is that thing made of? Even after attacking so many times... it’s still perfectly fine. Only two of them broken.’","And even those two had been broken because the creature’s body, while avoiding them, had somehow brushed against them..","And then her pupils contracted. The floor was still standing. She had just unleashed an attack capable of devastating an enormous area.","Other than small damage, everything was standing still. It was same as before. While the land and forest surrouding it was destroyed.","While the unknown creature’s body was still covered in smoke and dust.","WHOOSH!","Something suddenly shot through the smoke.","Akari immediately twisted her body. A tentacle passed where her head had been.","Nearly hundreds of black-red tentacles shot toward Akari.","Her eyes widened.","WHOOSH! WHOOSH! WHOOSH!","Tentacles erupted from the battlefield in every direction. They moved faster than before. The abomination’s corrupted flesh was producing them continuously.","They spread across the ground, through the trees, and into the sky. Some wrapped around mountains. Others tore through the earth.","Everywhere they touched began to decay.","Akari flew backward, narrowly avoiding one after another.","It’s getting faster. The dust finally disappeared. The abomination emerged. Its body was regenerating.","But something had changed. Its flesh was reconstructing itself faster than before.","And its body was larger. Much larger than before.","Akari’s heart sank. It’s becoming stronger. She looked across the battlefield.","The crimson corruption continued spreading. Then her gaze shifted toward the direction Noah had escaped.","Her expression changed.","’Noah.’","The tentacles were spreading toward him. Akari immediately understood the situation.","She might not be able to kill this creature. Perhaps not even with her strongest attacks.","But she couldn’t allow it to reach Noah. Her wings slowly spread. Lightning gathered around her body.","’If killing it isn’t possible...’","Her eyes became sharp. She couldn’t stay here.","’Then I’ll have to protect him somehow.’","She glanced once more at the abomination.","’I need to get Noah farther away.’ She thought.","The creature suddenly roared.","GWRROOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOWL!!!","Thousands of tentacles surged outward.","Akari turned toward Noah’s direction. Her body became enveloped in blue lightning. Two wings appeared behind.","KRAK!","Then she vanished. A streak of azure crossed the crimson sky.","Because this time, Akari wasn’t fighting to destroy her enemy. Now she was fighting to make sure the person she cared about survived.","Her only thought was Noah.","’I need to get him farther away. Somewhere safe.. anywhere.’","She had barely covered a few kilometers when.","WHOOSH!","Something moved beneath her.","Akari’s eyes widened in shock.","A gigantic tentacle erupted from the ground and wrapped around her waist before she could react.","\"—What?!\""]},{"number":294,"title":"Chapter 294: Is There No Other Way? [1]","paragraphs":["The tentacle tightened. Then another wrapped around her wing. And another caught her leg.","BOOOOOOM!!!","Akari was violently dragged downward. Her enormous body slammed into the earth with enough force to create a massive crater.","The impact shattered trees and sent mud, rocks, and debris flying in every direction.","\"AAAAAAARGH!!!\"","A scream tore from her throat. This wasn’t ordinary pain. The moment the corrupted flesh touched her scales, it began to erode them.","HISSSSSSS!","Her sapphire scales darkened. Then they began to crumble.","The corrupted energy seeped through the gaps between them, eating away at everything it touched in faster speed.","Akari writhed desperately. Lightning exploded from her body.","KRAK! KRAK!","The surrounding tentacles burned, but several remained attached. Pain spread through her entire body. She had never felt this much pain before. It was too much.","Every point of contact felt as though her flesh were being dissolved from the inside.","\"AAARGH!\"","Her eyes filled with agony. She had endured countless injuries throughout her life.","She had broken bones, burns, deep wounds. But this was different. The corruption wasn’t simply damaging her.","It was destroying her existence layer by layer.","Akari gritted her teeth.","’I can’t stay here.’","She released her dragon form. Blue light enveloped her enormous body.","FLASH!","Her gigantic dragon form collapsed into a human figure. The tentacles briefly lost their grip.","Akari immediately took advantage of it. Lightning erupted from her back.","BOOM!","She shot into the sky. She didn’t look back. She couldn’t afford to. Her body was screaming in pain with every movement.","’Noah...’","She forced herself forward. More than thirty kilometers separated them. Normally, that distance would have taken time.","For Akari, however, it took less than a minute. She crossed the distance as a blue streak through the storm.","BOOM!","She descended near Noah. He was running and immediately turned. His eyes widened.","\"Akari?!\"","She staggered in midair before landing unsteadily. Her condition was horrifying.","Her violet-blue kimono was torn and partially melted away.","Dark patches covered parts of her arms, shoulders, waist, and legs.","Where the corrupted tentacles had touched her, her skin had become blackened and sticky, as though it had partially decomposed.","Small pieces of damaged skin continued to crumble away.","Akari’s breathing was ragged.","\"Haa... haa...\"","Noah rushed toward her.","\"Akari!\"","\"I’m... fine.\"","Her voice trembled despite her attempt to sound composed.","Noah froze. His eyes widened as he looked at the injuries covering her body.","He got closer and held her by shoulder.","\"You... you’re not fine.\"","Akari clenched her teeth. She glanced back toward the distant storm. The horizon was still glowing crimson.","\"Listen to me.\"","Her breathing remained heavy.","\"I need to get you farther away.\"","\"Is there no other way.\" He asked while looking at her condition. He was looking at the battle from time to time.","They were huge so even from this long distance it was visible. She had been trapped by monster’s tentacles. Only for few seconds. And her body was already in such condition.","\"Noah—\"","\"I’m not leaving you.\" He shook his head.","Akari stared at him. His expression was serious. He was not ready to get away.","Fear appeared clearly in her eyes.","Not fear for herself. Fear for him.","\"I’ll protect you. I have to.\"","She forced herself upright despite the pain.","Lightning slowly gathered around her trembling body.","She lifted Noah and flew into the sky, looking down at the destruction below.","She held him in a princess carry. Under normal circumstances, he would have been embarrassed. But not right now.","He looked down at the destruction in terror.","The same went for Akari.","\"He wants to destroy this entire dimension,\" Noah said.","He watched as the monster spread its tentacles throughout the land, emerging from the surface and even from beneath the ground. Like enormous roots, they spread in every direction, destroying everything in their path.","In a few minutes, they would cover the entire dimension.","And with every passing second, their speed seemed to increase.","Both Noah and Akari stared at the destruction with fear and helplessness.","’This is... What can we even do? Nothing?’ Noah thought.","All he had done was watch the battle.","But even Akari’s powers seemed useless against this monster.","Was there anything they could do? Anything at all to survive?","\"It appears we don’t have a chance, Noah.\"","For the first time, Noah heard a tremble in Akari’s voice.","She stared at everything before them.","The hope and confidence she had once possessed,the certainty that they would escape this dimension, this realm, now seemed impossible.","She swallowed hard. The pain she had been feeling was no longer noticeable.","Everything had been swallowed by her helplessness.","Noah could see it in her eyes.","He looked back at the monster.","The abomination wasn’t even looking at them.","It already knew that, eventually, it would swallow them along with everything else.","’Noah! Think! Think! There has to be something that can help us get out of here! How did Damien handle it?’","Noah couldn’t bear seeing Akari like this.","He desperately went over everything he knew about the situation.","’What did Damien have that night that repelled this creature...? Light Mana? His Solar Core contained pure Light Mana, which was similar to the divine energy of the Sun God.’","He finally realized it.","’No wonder. Damien was destined to come here and escape this place. Maybe he was even destined to defeat it.’","His heart sank.","’So... there’s really no chance for us to get out?’","Even Noah began to feel helpless.","As he watched the endless destruction spreading across the dimension, he felt as though there was nothing he could do. Nothing at all.","The sky slowly turned more red an darker shade. Everything was crumbling.","Then his eyes went to the portal from which the creatures and monsters had emerged.","’What if...?’","A possibility suddenly occurred to him.","’No... If the other side is the monsters’ world... that would be suicide.’","Noah thought more deeply about it.","Then his gaze shifted toward Akari.","\"Akari!\"","His voice pulled her out of her own fear and helplessness.","\"What?\"","He looked into her blue eyes, which were still filled with fear.","\"What do you think is on the other side of that portal?\"","Akari frowned and turned her gaze toward the portal in the distance.","The enormous horizontal, circular portal hovered above the gray floor, surrounded by the ruins and destruction left in its wake.","\"I... don’t know,\" she admitted. \"It could be the realm that unknown creature came from... or...\"","\"Or?\"","Akari’s expression became more serious.","\"While fighting the monster, two red crystals were destroyed by my attack and that creature’s corruption, and that portal has been open for this long, so there’s another possibility.\"","Noah’s eyes narrowed.","\"What possibility?\"","\"The portal may no longer be simply connecting two fixed points.\"","She pointed toward the enormous gateway.","\"Think about what happens when a portal remains open. It continuously forces two separate locations to overlap. The longer it remains active, the greater the spatial distortion around it becomes unless you are providing continuous energy to it.\"","Noah’s expression hardened.","Akari continued.","\"If the other side really is another realm, then the portal isn’t merely connecting two places. It’s connecting two different spaces entirely. And if that connection has been left open for long enough... and few crystals which were keeping it open and stable has been destroyed.\"","She paused.","\"...the boundary between our dimension and theirs could have become dangerously thin.\"","Noah’s eyes widened slightly.","\"You mean...\"","\"Yes.\"","Akari stared at the portal.","\"The two realms could have been pulled closer together through space itself. The portal might have started as nothing more than a doorway between two points, but after what happened, the distortion could have expanded beyond the original gateway.\"","She swallowed.","\"And if that’s true...\"","Noah finished her thought. \"Then the portal might not be the only place where the two realms are connected anymore. We could see the space between it... or say dimensional tunnel.\"","Akari nodded grimly."]},{"number":295,"title":"Chapter 295: Is There No Other Way? [2]","paragraphs":["\"So, what should we do?\" Noah asked.","Akari remained silent for several seconds, staring at the crimson portal in the distance.","\"We can try entering it,\" she finally said. \"It’s the only option I can see right now.\"","\"And what happens after we enter?\" Noah asked.","\"I don’t know.\"","Noah frowned.","Akari continued, \"But there might be some kind of dimensional passage connected to it. If that portal is linking this realm to another space, then there should be a boundary between the two.\"","She looked toward the swirling crimson vortex.","\"If the connection between the two spaces is unstable, that boundary might have been damaged. There could be a temporary passage between them, a space that exists between this realm and wherever that portal leads.\"","\"And if we reach that passage?\"","\"I might be able to tear through the dimensional boundary and create another exit.\"","Akari’s expression became serious.","\"It wouldn’t necessarily take us to the same place as the portal. We could end up somewhere completely unknown. Another realm... or even another dimension.\"","\"So we’d be escaping through an unknown dimensional space?\"","\"Possibly.\"","Noah stared at her.","Akari took a slow breath before continuing.","\"But there’s a serious problem.\"","\"What?\"","\"Entering a dimensional passage isn’t like walking through a normal tunnel.\"","Her gaze returned to the crimson portal.","\"Inside, space itself may not behave normally. The distance between two points could constantly shift. The boundary could collapse or distort without warning. If that happens while we’re inside, the spatial force could tear our bodies apart.\"","Noah’s expression hardened.","\"Meaning?\"","\"Meaning we could be partially disintegrated... or worse.\"","Akari paused.","\"Different parts of our bodies could be displaced into different spatial coordinates. If that happens, there’s no guarantee we’ll even come out in one piece.\"","She looked down at her trembling hands.","\"And after what happened to me, I don’t think my body is strong enough to withstand that kind of spatial distortion for long even if I am a dragon now.\"","Her eyes shifted toward Noah.","\"And protecting you at the same time would make it even harder.\"","Noah glanced toward the distant battlefield.","The crimson corruption continued spreading through the forest.","Tentacles covered the ground like a massive, living network, tearing through everything in their path.","\"We really don’t have any better options, do we?\" Noah asked quietly.","Akari shook her head.","\"No.\"","A moment of silence followed.","\"Then let’s do it. The longer we wait, the worse this will become.\" Noah spoke.","\"Agreed.\"","Blue lightning immediately enveloped Akari’s body. She reached out and pulled Noah into her arms, securing him against her chest.","\"Hold on tightly.\"","\"Got it.\"","KRAK!","Akari vanished.","She became nothing more than a streak of blue light cutting through the storm. Within seconds, the landscape blurred beneath them.","Trees became indistinct shadows. The distance disappeared rapidly. But the abomination noticed.","Its enormous eye turned toward them. A low, distorted growl rolled across the battlefield.","BOOOOOOM!","The earth exploded. Hundreds of enormous tentacles erupted from the ground.","They rose like black-red serpents, twisting toward the sky and converging on Akari’s path.","Akari’s eyes narrowed.","\"Tch.\"","She immediately changed direction. A tentacle passed within meters of her.Another came from the side.","She tilted her body. It missed. Another descended from above. Akari twisted sideways while keeping one arm firmly wrapped around Noah.","WHOOSH!","The tentacle tore past them.","Noah felt the violent wind against his face. She was moving so fast that he couldn’t see anything well. But he could still understand what was happening.","\"There’s too many!\"","\"I know.\"","Akari accelerated.","Her speed was tremendous.","She weaved between the tentacles with impossible precision, constantly changing direction.","Left, right, up and down.","Every movement was calculated around one priority.","Don’t let anything touch Noah. Then Akari noticed something.","Her expression changed. The air itself was beginning to distort. A faint crimson haze surrounded the battlefield.","It wasn’t merely smoke. The corruption had spread into the atmosphere.","Akari flew through it. Immediately, her skin began to sting.","It’s even in the air now. The corrupted energy wasn’t strong enough to destroy her instantly, but it was slowly eating away at her defenses.","Her breathing became slightly heavier. Her lightning flickered. She clenched her teeth.","’I can’t slow down.’","\"Noah... the air... it’s dangerous.\" She whispered to him.","Noah hearing it, held his breath.","Another tentacle shot toward them.","Akari accelerated.","WHOOSH!","It missed Noah by inches. She twisted around another.","The speed at that creature was moving had increased by a lot.","CRACK!","A tentacle came from beneath them. Ot was too fast.","Even Akari who was flying, moving like flash couldn’t dodge without exposing Noah.","She turned her body instead.","BOOM!","The tentacle struck her back. Akari’s body jerked violently.","\"Akari!\"","She gritted her teeth and refused to release him. Blood trickled from the corner of her mouth.","\"I’m fine.\"","She accelerated again. Another tentacle approached.","Akari swung her free hand.","KRAK!","Lightning exploded outward, slicing the tentacle apart. But the severed flesh immediately began regenerating.","More appeared behind it. Akari’s expression became grim.","It won’t stop. Her wings spread. A massive burst of wind erupted around her, pushing dozens of tentacles away.","For a moment, a path opened.","\"Now!\"","She shot forward. The portal was getting closer. But the tentacles suddenly changed direction.","Instead of attacking them directly, they began forming a wall around the portal’s entrance.","Akari’s eyes widened.","\"They’re blocking the entrance...\"","The entire area ahead had become a fortress of writhing corrupted flesh.","Tentacles intertwined with one another, creating layer after layer.","No clear path remained. Akari tightened her hold around Noah.","\"I’ll make one.\"","Her lightning intensified. She accelerated directly toward the mass.","Noah looked up at her.","\"Akari, your body—\"","\"I know.\"","Her skin was already showing fresh darkened patches.","Several wounds had reopened. Blood stained her torn kimono. But she didn’t stop.","She raised her free hand. A massive sphere of lightning formed around them.","KRAAAAAAAAAK!","The lightning sphere exploded forward. Tentacles were blasted apart.","For several seconds, they had a path. Akari flew through it. But the corrupted flesh regenerated almost immediately.","A tentacle emerged from the side and struck her shoulder.","SPLAT!","Blood scattered through the air. Akari’s body trembled. Yet her arms remained locked around Noah.","She protected his head against her chest and twisted her body so the impact hit her instead.","\"Akari!\"","\"Don’t worry about me.\"","Her voice was strained.","\"Just hold on. I won’t let anything happen to you.\"","More tentacles like it’s arms descended.","Akari dodged one. But there were simply too many. He body was already weakened. One wrapped around her ankle.","She immediately severed it with lightning. Another struck her side. Another grazed her back.","Her skin continued to burn and decompose wherever the corruption touched her.","Still, she kept moving. Still, Noah remained completely protected within her arms.","Finally, the portal was directly ahead.","Only a few hundred meters remained. Akari stared at the swirling crimson vortex.","Her breathing became ragged. Her body was reaching its limit. But her grip around Noah tightened.","\"We’re almost there.\""]},{"number":296,"title":"Chapter 296: They Cannot Let Me Die!!","paragraphs":["The portal was close.","So close that Akari could almost feel the strange dimensional energy brushing against her body.","’We’re going to make it.’","For the first time since the abomination had emerged, a faint glimmer of hope appeared in her heart.","If they could just cross that portal, perhaps they could escape this nightmare. There was a chance after all.","WHOOSH!","The ground ahead erupted.","More tentacles emerged from beneath the corrupted earth.","Their blackish-red flesh split open.","One after another, grotesque red eyes appeared within them. They stared directly at Akari and Noah.","Their gaze were hungry, murderous, waiting. Then the flesh surrounding those eyes tore apart.","SQUELCH!","Countless mouths opened. Rows of irregular teeth emerged from the rotten flesh.","And then something released from them.","\"HEEHEEHEEHEEHEEHEE!\"","Laughter echoed across the forest, not from one mouth but from dozens, hundreds.","The sound overlapped until it became an unbearable chorus of madness.","Akari’s expression changed.","\"What—?\"","HAAAAA!","Every mouth exhaled simultaneously. A massive wave of crimson smoke surged toward them.","Akari immediately tried to accelerate. It was too late. The smoke swallowed them.","\"AAAAARGH!\"","\"ARRRGHHH!\"","Both Noah and Akari screamed.","The pain was immediate. It felt as though countless needles had been driven into their skin at once.","Akari’s flesh began darkening. The corruption seeped beneath her skin, eating away at it.","Even her newly awakened dragon body couldn’t completely resist it.","Noah wasn’t spared either. His exposed skin rott faster then hers. Dark patches spread across his arms and face.","His blue eyes became bloodshot, tears streaming uncontrollably from them.","\"NO!\"","Akari looked at him. Forgetting her own pain, she immediately released an enormous amount of mana.","KRAK!","A layer of blue lightning and mana enveloped Noah completely.","The crimson smoke struck the barrier.","HISSSSSSS!","It began eating through it. Now it was slowly, but it was enough.","Akari gritted her teeth.","\"Hold on!\"","She forced more mana into the barrier. But her speed had already dropped. Her body was becoming weaker.","WHOOSH!","A tentacle came from her blind side.","Akari’s eyes widened. She couldn’t dodge while protecting Noah. So she made her choice. She turned her body to other side.","BOOOOOOM!","The tentacle slammed directly into her back. She took the hit, only on her.","\"ARGH!\"","Blood sprayed from her mouth. The impact sent her crashing downward.","She fell through the corrupted air before finally landing in one of the few remaining clear patches of ground.","BOOM!","The earth cracked beneath her. Yet her arms never opened.","Noah remained safely held against her chest.","Akari’s breathing became ragged from exhaustion and pain.","\"Haa... haa...\"","Noah coughed violently.","\"Cough! Cough!\"","He slowly lifted his head.","\"A-Akari...\"","She looked at him. Her beautiful face was no longer untouched.","Parts of her cheek had become blackened and damaged, the corrupted energy eating away at her skin.","But her eyes her eyes remained the same. They were clear blue color. As beautiful as always.","But now they filled with tears.","Noah stared at them.","’She’s crying.’","A tear rolled down Akari’s cheek, then another.","\"I... I’m sorry, Noah.\" Her voice trembled. She could no longer hold back her pain, her sadness, her crumbling hope.","\"I couldn’t protect you.\"","\"No...\" Noah replied, trying to tell her she was not at fault.","\"Even after everything...\" Her tears continued falling. \"I had so much power...\"","She lowered her gaze. \"Yet I still couldn’t protect you.\"","She sniffed in shame and defeat.","Noah’s chest tightened.","\"N-No, Akari...\"","Before he could finish. Tentacles came to attack them.They didn’t stop even after harming them so much.","BOOOOOOM!","But Noah didn’t let them come so fast. Huge walls of ice erupted from the ground around them. The incoming tentacles crashed against them.","CRACK!","The first wall shattered. Another rose immediately, then another.","Noah’s remaining mana poured into the defenses.","His body trembled from exhaustion. But he forced himself upright.","\"Don’t apologize...\"","Akari looked at him.","Noah slowly reached toward her face. His fingers gently touched the damaged skin on her cheek.","\"Don’t... apologize to me.\"","His voice was weak. But he stilltry to keep a gentle tone.","\"But... we won’t die here.\"","Another wall shattered. The tentacles pushed closer.","Noah pulled Akari into his arms.","\"N-Noah?\"","\"We’re getting out.\"","His body trembled violently.","\"We have to get out!!\"","He tightened his embrace. \"You still have to meet your daughter.\"","A faint smile appeared on his damaged face.","\"And scold her...\"","He coughed.","\"...for me.\"","Akari’s lips trembled.","\"You’re still thinking about that...?\"","\"Of course.\"","His breathing became heavier.","\"We promised each other that we’d get out together.\"","The last ice wall shattered.","BOOOOOOM!","Tentacles surged toward them.","Noah slowly stood. His legs trembled but he still pushed himself.","His legs nearly gave out. Akari tried to rise as well, but her body refused to cooperate. So he held her in his arms, supporting her to stand up.","\"Noah...\"","He gaze at her face. He wanted to save her, protect her. But he was too weak. What could he even do?","He clenched his teeth.","He looked ahead. The world seemed strangely slow. The tentacles moved toward them.","The crimson smoke drifted through the air. The corrupted forest burned beneath the storm.","His heartbeat grew louder.","Ba-dump.","His eyelids became heavy.","Ba-dump.","No, he clenched his fist. This shouldn’t end here. His thoughts became chaotic.","’The system... There has to be something. Someone... Something... someone brought me here... so they have to protect me!! They cannot let me die!!’","His head slowly tilted upward.","The sky had changed. The crimson clouds were beginning to separate. And for the first time in what felt like an eternity.","The rain had stopped. Silence descended. A gap appeared between the clouds.","Soft, pale light poured through it.","Noah’s eyes widened. A familiar celestial glow appeared above the battlefield. It wasn’t sunlight. It wasn’t lightning.","It was softer. It was colder, like ice. Beautiful, like some calm cold.","His pupils trembled. He stared at the glowing sphere emerging between the clouds.","At this moment, all he could think about was that single person.","His lips slowly parted.","\"Moon...\"","The moment he whispered that single word, everything went silent.","---","[A/N:Hello guys!! Finally coming to last part of this arc!!]"]},{"number":297,"title":"Chapter 297: Moon [1]","paragraphs":["Noah blinked. For a moment, he couldn’t understand what had happened.","The overwhelming pain was gone. The screams had vanished. Even the oppressive presence of the abomination had disappeared.","He slowly looked down at his hands.They were trembling slightly.","\"Haaah...\"","A soft breath escaped his lips, turning into a faint cloud of frost in the cold air.","\"Akari?\"","There was no answer. His expression changed. He immediately looked around.","She wasn’t there.","Noah stood completely alone in the middle of a vast, barren landscape.","The ground beneath his feet was gray and lifeless, stretching endlessly toward the horizon.","Massive mountains rose in the distance, their surfaces covered in the same dull gray stone. Countless craters and enormous rocks were scattered across the landscape.","There wasn’t a single tree, not a blade of grass and not even the slightest sign of life.","Noah slowly raised his head. His breath caught. There was no sky. Instead, an endless expanse of darkness stretched above him.","And within that darkness countless stars.","Millions upon millions of them glittered across the infinite void, shining with a beauty that Noah had witnessed before.","This place was familiar.","The ground beneath his feet gave off a faint, soothing silver glow, illuminating the barren landscape just enough to reveal its strange beauty.","Noah’s eyes widened. He had seen this place before.","\"The Moon.\"","His voice came out as a whisper.","\"I’m on the Moon.\"","A voice echoed through the empty realm.","\"Hmm. You recalled me.\"","The voice was calm and ancient, yet somehow carried a strange warmth.","\"For help.\"","Noah immediately turned around.","There was no one.","\"That means you encountered the Monarch of Decay again.\"","His pupils contracted.","\"You... already knew?\"","\"Of course.\"","The voice remained tranquil.","\"I had expected this and waiting for this moment.\"","Noah’s expression became complicated. She expected this? Before he could ask anything, the mysterious voice continued.","\"Do not worry, child. I will help you survive.\"","A brief pause followed.","\"And I will help you save your partner.\"","Noah’s eyes widened.","\"Akari... But you must do something for me in return.\"","Noah looked around desperately.","\"What do you want?\"","There was no response for several seconds.","\"You will know when the time comes.\"","Noah clenched his fists. There were countless questions filling his mind.","Who was she? Why was she helping him? How did she know about the Monarch of Decay?","And what exactly did she want from him? But none of those questions mattered right now.","Akari was still out there. Possibly one verge of dying.","\"I’ll do it.\"","His answer came without hesitation.","\"I’ll do whatever you want.\"","He couldn’t afford to hesitate. He couldn’t accept dying here. And more importantly he couldn’t let Akari die there.","\"Good...\"","The mysterious voice seemed pleased.","\"I will tell you what you must do when the time comes.\"","A strange warmth suddenly surrounded Noah.","His eyelids became heavy. His body grew strangely light. He didn’t feel afraid. Instead, an inexplicable sense of calm washed over him.","He slowly closed his eyes.","\"Haa...\"","He exhaled. He opened them.","---","BOOOOOOM!!!","Noah returned. The world exploded back into existence. The corrupted forest. The crimson sky. The endless storm.","The countless tentacles, the abomination controlling them. Everything had returned. Yet something was different.","Everything around him seemed incredibly slow. The tentacles moved as though they were crawling through water.","Falling debris hung suspended in the air. Even the crimson energy spreading across the ground appeared almost motionless.","In his arms held Akari. Her breathing was slowed.","Noah slowly raised his head. His eyes were no longer their usual blue. They now shone with an intense blue-silver radiance.","---","The entire realm had become a nightmare. Black tentacles covered the landscape like an enormous living web.","Countless pale, oily creatures crawled between them, their distorted bodies twisted into unnatural shapes.","Everything was dying. Trees collapsed into dust. Grass withered like they never existed. Rocks cracked and crumbled.","The very earth itself was slowly rotting. The once-beautiful forest had disappeared beneath an ocean of corruption.","Above it all, the sky had turned crimson. The air was saturated with the vile energy radiating from the abomination.","And countless eyes had opened across the monstrous tentacles. All of them suddenly turned toward the same location.","The center of the corrupted realm.","For a moment everything stopped.","BOOOOOOOOOOM!!!","A tremendous shockwave erupted from the center. The corrupted ground cracked outward. Tentacles were blasted away.","The surrounding creatures were thrown into the air.","And from the heart of the explosion something silver emerged. A small sphere of pale light floated above the ground.","It pulsed once.","THUM.","Silver radiance spread outward.","The nearest tentacles instantly froze. Their writhing movements stopped as a layer of crystalline frost covered their rotten flesh.","The sphere expanded with every second, it grew larger. And the faster it expanded, the faster the freezing spread.","Tentacles became frozen statues. The twisted creatures were trapped beneath layers of silver-white ice.","Even the crimson energy surrounding the area began to recede wherever the silver radiance touched.","The entire realm trembled. Then the sphere expanded beyond the forest.","Beyond the mountains. Its radiance illuminated the crimson sky.","Until finally a gigantic silver moon started floated above the corrupted realm. Its surface shimmered with pale light.","Its presence was strangely beautiful and peaceful.","Yet beneath that tranquility was an overwhelming power that made even the corruption itself tremble.","The enormous moon continued to expand.","And its silver radiance continued spreading across the dying realm.","The Monarch of Decay had encountered something that made its countless eyes turn toward the moon in alarm.","The moon floated above, it’s gentle radiance spread across the realm, pushing back the crimson smoke that had covered the heavens.","Wherever the silver light reached, the decay receded.","The suffocating red sky gradually cleared, revealing the endless darkness and distant stars beyond it.","The abomination reacted violently. Countless mouths opened across its grotesque body.","\"WHY?!\"","Its voice thundered across the entire realm.","\"WHY ARE YOU HERE?! WHY ARE YOU INTERFERING IN MY WAY?!\"","The roar shook the earth. There was no answer.","The moon simply continued to rise. Then, atop the enormous silver moon stood a young man.","His once-dirty white hair had become brilliant white, glowing faintly beneath the moon’s radiance. A layer of mysterious silver energy surrounded his body like a thin veil of light.","His eyes were no longer the familiar blue. They shone with a cold, silver-blue brilliance.","Like frost beneath moonlight.","Noah slowly lowered himself and carefully placed Akari onto the surface of the moon.","She barely opened her eyes.","Her breathing was weak, her body covered in injuries. Even in her human form, traces of corruption remained across her skin spread widely while protecting him.","She looked at Noah through half-lidded eyes.","\"Noah...\"","He glanced at her.","\"Rest.\"","His voice was calm. After making sure she was safely lying down, Noah slowly stood.","He looked at his hands. Silver light flowed across his fingers.","It wasn’t mana. He could immediately tell the difference. Mana felt familiar, something that originated from within his own body and responded to his will.","This energy was completely different.","It felt ancient and too pure. And impossibly vast.","Noah narrowed his eyes.","’This feeling...’","He remembered Damien. The energy surrounding Damien whenever he used his blessing.","’Divine energy.’","But there was a fundamental difference. Damien’s divine energy had felt warm. Almost like sunlight.","This energy was too cold. Like the endless night itself.","’So this is the Divine Energy of the Moon Goddess. She’s helping me directly?’","Noah slowly clenched his fist.","BOOM!","The surrounding space trembled slightly.","His eyes widened. The abomination that had terrified him moments ago.","Suddenly seemed insignificant. Like a tiny insect beneath his feet.","Noah looked down. The creature was still growing.","Its enormous body continued expanding, feeding upon the vitality from surrounding.","Yet Noah no longer felt fear.","CRACK.","A strange sound came from above.","Noah raised his head. His expression changed.","A thin crack had appeared across the sky.","CRACK... CRACK...","Space itself was beginning to fracture. The entire dimension was reaching its limit.","The Monarch of Decay wasn’t merely destroying the forest anymore. Its presence was destabilizing the entire realm.","The dimension itself was beginning to collapse.","Noah’s gaze returned to the abomination.","The countless mouths across its body opened once again.","\"IT DOESN’T MATTER!\"","Its voice shook the heavens.","\"I WILL KILL YOU!\"","WHOOSH! WHOOSH! WHOOSH!","An immeasurable number of enormous tentacles erupted from every direction.They surged toward the silver moon like an endless black tide.","At the same time, countless mouths opened across their surfaces. Crimson energy began gathering within them.","BOOOOOOM!","Streams of red energy that could decay anything shot toward Noah from every direction.","The attacks were so numerous that they seemed to cover the entire sky.","Yet Noah didn’t move. He simply stood there watching.","The tentacles drew closer. They were almost touching the moon.","Noah finally raised his right hand. His expression remained completely indifferent. Then he casually swung his hand toward the approaching horde.","SHIIIIING!","Silver radiance erupted.","In an instant.","CRACK! CRACK! CRACK!","Kilometres of tentacles froze simultaneously. Silver-blue frost raced through their enormous bodies at an impossible speed.","The black-crimson flesh hardened. The countless eyes froze in place. Even the crimson energy inside the mouths became trapped in crystalline ice.","Within a single breath, the endless tide of tentacles surrounding the moon had become a gigantic frozen sculpture."]},{"number":298,"title":"Chapter 298: MOON [2]","paragraphs":["The frost continued to spread into the small world like blizzard had appeared.","It raced across the ground, climbed the trees, and crawled over the countless tentacles that had invaded the realm.","The once crimson sky gradually faded away. Red clouds by rotten energy turned silver.","The thick, corrupted atmosphere was replaced by an overwhelming coldness. Every breath carried a faint mist, and the wind became so frigid that even the remaining corruption began to disappear.","The vile energy that had poisoned the air for so long was being purified simply by coming into contact with the divine radiance.","At the center of it all, the enormous silver moon remained suspended in the heavens.","The moon remained silent, beautiful and untouchable to anyone else other than person standing on it.","The abomination stared at it. Its remaining eyes trembled with anger, hatred—and something it had never shown before.","There was fear. Large portions of its grotesque body had been frozen solid. Everything near the moon had been transformed into crystal-clear ice, trapping its rotten flesh beneath layers of silver-blue frost.","Noah slowly raised his hand. Divine energy surged through his body. The silver radiance gathered within his palm before rapidly condensing.","SHIIING!","A sword materialized.","Its blade was formed entirely from ice created by the divine coldness. It wasn’t ordinary frost. The blade seemed to contain the very essence of the moon’s frigid power.","Noah wrapped his fingers around the hilt.","The moment he did,","BOOM!","An invisible pressure erupted from his body. He felt stronger than he had ever felt before. Not merely stronger. He felt as though his very existence had been elevated to another level.","He knew that this was not his powers, it was given by someone else. Yet they didn’t felt unknown.","’Or... this freezing powers related to my bloodline? Maybe... Her divine energy only helped me to use them for temporary.’","Noah slowly raised the sword above his head. His white hair fluttered in the freezing wind with smooth motion.","His silver aura illuminated the darkness around him. His expression remained completely emotionless. His skin turned pale milky white. As if he posses no blood in his body.","There was no anger in him. There was no hatred for the creature. Nor there was any desire for revenge. All remained inside him was cold indifference.","As if the terrifying creature before him wasn’t even worthy of provoking an emotion.","\"It’s your end, Monarch of Decay.\"","His voice was quiet. Yet it echoed throughout the dying realm.","The abomination’s countless mouths opened.","\"YOU DARE THREATEN ME?!\"","Its roar shook the remaining mountains.","Noah didn’t even blink. He simply stared at it.","Then he moved. There was no reason for him to waste time. It should end as fast as possible.","BOOOOOOM!","The enormous silver moon above him suddenly trembled.","The abomination froze. Every remaining eye turned upward. Terror appeared within them at the sight in front of them.","But then those eyes shifted, not toward the moon but toward the figure standing upon it.","As if he had sense something from the man. Something similar to them. Not the divine energy of the moon, but something different.","Then it clicked to monarch of decay.","\"...A... Monarch?\"","The creature’s voice trembled for the first time.","Then behind the moon, an enormous silver silhouette slowly emerged. It was shaped like a woman.","A veil concealed her face, while her colossal hands appeared beneath the moon, as though she were gently holding it between her palms.","Her presence alone caused the entire dimension to tremble. Noah remained completely still. Not aware of what decay was watching. Then he moved.","His sword descended.","SWIISH!","It was a one elegant motion. The movement was simple, precise. Almost effortless, yet behind that single slash was an immeasurable amount of divine power.","A thin silver line appeared across the moon.","After that silence followed. Nothing happened.","The Decay’s countless pupils moved around. It was completely helpless.","CRACK.","A fracture appeared across its surface.","CRACK! CRACK! CRACK!","Countless cracks rapidly spread across the enormous moon, branching in every direction like a web.","Akari, who had barely managed to stand, stared upward in disbelief.","\"Noah...\"","The moon began to glow. Brilliant silver light poured through every crack. The entire realm became illuminated. For one fleeting moment, everything was silent.","But that silence was just a calm before the storm.","BOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOM!!!","The moon exploded. A colossal pillar of silver divine energy erupted from its shattered core.","There was no heat within it.","Only cold.","A primordial coldness so absolute that even the surrounding space seemed to freeze.","The pillar descended upon the forest and the mountains. The corrupted earth was pierced by it.","And finally, The Monarch of Decay.","\"ARRRRRGHHHHHHHHHH!!!\"","Its scream echoed throughout the realm. Its enormous body struggled against the pillar, countless tentacles thrashing wildly.","But the divine cold consumed everything. Its rotten flesh froze. Its countless mouths shattered.","Its eyes disappeared beneath layers of silver ice. Even the corruption sustaining its body was extinguished. The pillar continued expanding in kilometers non stop.","The entire pocket dimension was swallowed by silver radiance in freezing coldness. Everything froze inside it, not explode.","CRACK.","Space fractured rapidly.","CRACK! CRACK! CRACK!","The dimensional walls began collapsing. Frozen mountains broke apart with huge cracks. The ground shattered into countless fragments.","The sky itself split open. The pocket dimension could no longer withstand the force of the attack.","And finally the time for it’s end came.","BOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOM!!!","The entire realm collapsed. Not like destruction from an explosion. But it was as if everything froze and then shattered.","Everything disappeared into an endless explosion of silver light. The forest, the corruption and even the portal, they all vanished.","The Monarch of Decay. Even the dimension itself.","All of it ceased to exist.","And between all of this only Noah and Akira remained alive. Finally they had killed the creature.","Noah lost his consciousness and fell down, Akari saw it.","\"Noah!!\" She yelled and shot toward him as the world started to crumble."]},{"number":299,"title":"Chapter 299: Did They Survive?","paragraphs":["There was no ground, sky or air.","Noah’s body fell endlessly through a chaotic expanse of darkness with glowing waves of different colors in distance.","Silver-blue cracks stretched across the void like shattered glass, constantly appearing and disappearing around him.","Fragments of the destroyed realm drifted through the darkness as if the realm never existed.","Noah was unconscious. His body continued to tumble helplessly through the unstable dimensional space.","\"NOAH!\"","Akari’s voice rang through the darkness. She reached out and grabbed him before the dimensional current could separate them.","She was tired, but still moved to save Noah. She couldn’t let him go away from her. Her fingers tightly wrapped around his arm.","\"No... no, no...\"","She pulled his unconscious body against her.","The moment she did it.","BOOOOM!","A violent dimensional force struck them.","Akari’s body was sent spinning.","Pain immediately spread through her entire body. It felt as though countless invisible hands were trying to tear her apart.","Her clothes fluttered violently as her body was dragged toward a distant crack in space.","\"Urgh!\"","She gritted her teeth and held Noah even tighter. She couldn’t let go. She absolutely couldn’t.","If they were separated here. She didn’t know whether they would ever meet again. Then something awakened behind her.","FWOOSH!","Two enormous dragon wings erupted from her back. Their powerful wings immediately spread around them, forming a protective shell.","Akari curled her body around Noah and used her wings to cover both of them completely.","\"Stay with me...\"","Her voice trembled.","\"Noah... please.\"","She poured the remaining mana inside her body into her wings. A faint barrier formed around them.","The dimensional pressure weakened.","Akari’s eyes widened.","\"It worked...\"","But her relief lasted only a second.","CRACK!","The barrier trembled violently.","Akari’s expression changed. The force surrounding them was simply too powerful. This wasn’t ordinary wind. It wasn’t even ordinary magical pressure.","The space itself was unstable. Every dimensional current they passed through was trying to pull their bodies in different directions.","One force pulled her arm toward the darkness with different color waves. Another dragged her legs in the opposite direction.","Something twisted around her wings. Akari screamed as pain shot through her body.","\"AAAAH!\"","She desperately reinforced the barrier. More mana poured out of her body.","But there wasn’t much left. Her mana had already been nearly exhausted before they entered this place.","Still, she continued, she had no other choice.","\"If I stop...\"","Her trembling eyes moved toward Noah. His face was pale. His eyes remained closed.","\"...we’ll be torn apart.\"","She wrapped her wings even tighter around him. The dimensional currents grew stronger.","BOOM!","The barrier cracked.","Akari’s body slammed against Noah’s.","She grunted in pain but refused to release him, another dimensional wave struck.","CRACK!","A portion of her barrier shattered.","Akari’s pupils contracted.","\"No...\"","She immediately poured the last of her mana into the remaining barrier. Her breathing became ragged. Her body felt incredibly heavy.","Her wings trembled violently. The pressure was becoming unbearable.","She could feel it now. The dimensional space was beginning to affect her body directly.","Her skin stung. Her bones ached. Even her senses were becoming distorted. She could no longer tell which direction they were falling.","There was only darkness and some dimmed glowing waves of different colors.","And Noah in her arms.","Akari lowered her head and pressed her forehead against his.","\"Don’t you dare die...\"","Her voice was barely a whisper.","\"Please...\"","Another violent force struck them.","BOOOOOOM!","Akari’s wings shook violently. A thin crack appeared across one of them. She clenched her teeth.","Tears formed in the corners of her eyes from the pain.","But she still didn’t let go. Instead, she pulled Noah closer.","Her dragon wings completely covered his body.","\"If someone has to be torn apart...\"","She closed her eyes. Her consciousness slowly fading away.","\"...it won’t be you.\"","---","As Noah and Akari continued to fall through the dimensional void, the darkness around them suddenly trembled.","BOOM!","A massive portal abruptly opened beneath them. Something enormous emerged from within it. At first, it looked like a blazing sun breaking through the darkness.","Then its shape became clear. It was a colossal bird.","Its entire body radiated a brilliant white-orange light that illuminated the surrounding void.","Its feathers were pure white at their base, each one glowing with an ethereal radiance, while brilliant orange-gold flames danced along their edges.","Its long, elegant tail streamed behind it like several burning ribbons of fire. The flames shifted between molten gold, vivid orange, red and white-hot brilliance, leaving trails of sparks that disappeared into the darkness.","The crown of feathers atop its head burned like a living flame, rising elegantly above its head without consuming the white feathers beneath it.","Its enormous wings stretched outward.","They were vast enough to dwarf Noah and Akari several times over, covered in layers of luminous white feathers.","Along the tips of those wings burned brilliant orange-gold flames, flowing backward like blazing banners as the phoenix moved.","Its eyes opened. They glowed with the color of living fire.","The unknown bird let out a piercing cry.","\"KRAAAAAAAAA!\"","The shrill cry echoed strangely through the dimensional void. Its fiery eyes suddenly focused on the two tiny figures falling through the unstable darkness.","Noah and Akari.","The mythical creature tilted its head.","FWOOSH!","Its enormous wings spread wide. It shot through the dimensional void.","Despite its immense size, the phoenix moved with incredible speed, cutting through the chaotic currents of unstable space as though they were nothing more than gentle winds.","It reached Noah and Akari in an instant.","Akari barely had time to look up. Her eyes widened. A colossal white wing swept around them.","Then the other followed.","It folded its enormous wings around both of them, completely enveloping their bodies within a cocoon of radiant feathers and warm golden flames.","The violent dimensional currents immediately crashed against its wings. But the bird remained unmoved.","Its brilliant feathers burned brighter. The surrounding darkness was pushed back by its radiance.","For a moment, Noah and Akari were completely protected within the wings.","Then the it turned. Its massive body began descending toward the portal from which it had emerged.","With Noah and Akari safely enclosed within its wings, it plunged downward through the unstable void.","The portal grew closer.","FWOOSH!","The giant bird disappeared into the portal, carrying both of them with it. The portal flickered once.","Then vanished. The dimensional void returned to silence."]},{"number":300,"title":"Chapter 300: Monarch Of Destruction [1]","paragraphs":["Far away from the planet Terranis, where humans and countless other races lived, beyond their solar system and the familiar reach of civilization, lay an unknown region of deep space.","In that distant corner of the universe floated a massive planet of dark maroon.","It was an unnatural world.","There were no trees on the land of red and maroon. As far as one could see there were no oceans, no rivers nor clouds. It looked like huge red maroon desert.","There was not even a sun or moon to illuminate its surface.","The planet simply drifted through the endless darkness of space, surrounded by countless distant stars. Their faint light was barely enough to reveal the barren landscape below.","There was no breathable atmosphere here. There was no oxygen and warmth. No conditions that could sustain ordinary life. Yet something lived here.","WHOOOOSH!","Violent winds swept across the planet’s surface, carrying enormous waves of maroon sand. The sandstorm moved like an endless crimson blizzard, covering the barren land and eroding the strange rocks scattered across the planet.","At the center of this desolate world stood a colossal mountain.","Its surface was composed entirely of dark, maroon-colored stone. It rose hundreds of meters into the air, its peak disappearing into the swirling sand.","Near the summit was a massive cave. For a long while, nothing happened.","Then something came out of the cave, it was a sound.","Tap.","Tap.","Tap.","The sound of footsteps echoed from within the cave. Someone was walking out.","A man emerged from the darkness. He was enormous.","Standing nearly 210 centimeters tall, his broad shoulders and muscular physique made him look more like a warrior forged for battle than an ordinary human.","He appeared to be in his mid-thirties.","His black hair moved wildly in the violent wind, while a pair of dark crimson eyes gazed calmly into the endless void above.","Despite his intimidating presence, his features were remarkably handsome and mature. He stopped near the edge of the mountain.","The man looked upward. Millions of stars glittered across the vast darkness. Farther away, countless galaxies stretched across space like rivers of light.","He watched them silently. Then his lips moved.","\"So...\"","His deep voice was almost swallowed by the howling wind.","\"They’re finally out.\"","His crimson eyes narrowed slightly.","\"After fighting the Puppet of Decay.\"","For several seconds, he remained silent. Then a faint, mysterious smile appeared on his face.","He stepped forward.","Tap.","His foot reached the very edge of the mountain.","Below him stretched an endless sea of maroon sand. Above him was the infinite universe.","The man stood there alone, gazing into the distant stars as though he were waiting for something—or someone—to appear.","\"It went as I expected.\"","CRACK.","A faint sound echoed through the emptiness of space.","The man standing at the edge of the maroon mountain suddenly raised his head. His crimson eyes narrowed.","The man’s attention was no longer on the planet beneath him. He was staring into the vast darkness above.","Another sound followed.","CRACK.","This time, it was louder. Something was happening in space. The darkness itself seemed to fracture. A thin line appeared across the endless void.","The cracks spread rapidly, branching across the darkness like fractures appearing on a gigantic mirror.","The man’s expression changed. A faint smile appeared on his lips.","\"So...\" His voice was quiet. \"You actually came.\"","The cracks continued spreading.","Reality itself seemed unable to contain whatever was attempting to cross through.","BOOOOOOM!","Space shattered. A colossal crimson eye emerged from beyond the broken dimensional boundary.","It was enormous.","Its diameter alone stretched for several kilometers, and its blood-red surface was filled with countless dark veins.","The gigantic pupil at its center contracted as it immediately locked onto the lone man standing on the mountain.","Pure rage radiated from that eye. The surrounding space distorted beneath the pressure. Then something began pulling itself through the shattered dimensional opening.","First came an enormous hand. Then a grotesque torso. The creature continued emerging until its entire upper body floated above the planet.","It possessed a vaguely humanoid form, but calling it humanoid was almost an insult to the word. Its body was composed of enormous masses of rotten flesh.","Dark-red and black tissue continuously twisted and moved across its surface. Countless creatures had been fused into its body.","Some were embedded halfway into its flesh. Others had become little more than twisted limbs protruding from its torso.","Faces could be seen beneath the translucent layers of rotten tissue, their mouths opening and closing soundlessly.","Tentacles extended from its shoulders, back, and arms, drifting through space like enormous serpents.","The creature was so gigantic that its body covered a vast portion of the sky. It was nearly half the size of the maroon planet beneath it.","The moment it completely emerged, an oppressive aura swept across the world.","BOOOOOOM!","The planet trembled. Cracks spread across the barren ground. Even the enormous sandstorms were pushed away by the pressure.","Yet the black-haired man didn’t move. He simply stood there. His hands remained casually at his sides.","The enormous eye of the creature focused on him. Then its voice exploded through space.","\"IT WAS YOUR PLAN ALL ALONG!\"","The voice was so powerful that the surrounding space itself vibrated.","\"YOU SET THEM UP IN THAT PLACE!\"","The creature’s enormous body trembled with fury.","\"YOU DELIBERATELY CREATED THAT SITUATION AND MADE ME GO THERE!\"","Its voice became louder.","\"AND YOU KNEW THAT DAMN BOY WOULD WEAKEN ME!\"","The man listened calmly. Then he chuckled.","\"Well, well.\"","He lifted his head slightly.","\"It was your own mistake for falling into my trap.\"","His crimson eyes glimmered.","\"I didn’t force you to go there.\"","The creature’s countless mouths opened.","\"YOU BASTARD! WHY DID YOU DO THAT!!\"","A wave of murderous intent exploded from its body. \"JUST BECAUSE YOU ARE THE MONARCH OF DESTRUCTION DOESN’T MEAN I FEAR YOU!\"","The man’s smile disappeared.","The creature continued.","\"DO YOU THINK YOUR TITLE GIVES YOU THE RIGHT TO DO WHATEVER YOU WANT?!\"","Dark-red energy began leaking from its enormous body. It wasn’t ordinary energy. Something that seemed to corrupt the very fabric of space. Wherever that energy passed, the stars in the distance appeared distorted.","\"Because of you,\" the creature roared, \"that damn Moon Goddess interfered!\"","The black-haired man’s expression remained calm. Until the next words came.","\"And because of that boy and her... everything ruined. \"","But the Monarch of Decay wasn’t finished. \"And that’s not all. That boy even possessed bloodline of a monarch.\"","The man finally frowned.","Silence. Then man’s eyes widened slightly. A genuine shock crossed his face. The man’s pupils contracted.","\"What?\"","His voice was barely audible. The creature roar.","\"YOU HEARD ME.\"","He spoke further, \"That human isn’t merely carrying the blessing of a God.\"","Its gigantic eye stared directly at him. \"He possesses the bloodline of a Monarch.\"","The man’s expression became increasingly grim.","\"That wasn’t supposed to happen.\" he muttered.","He lowered his gaze. \"It was supposed to be a man blessed by the Sun.\"","His mind raced. Everything had been carefully calculated. The pieces had been placed. The conditions had been prepared.","The one who was supposed to enter that place had been chosen. The one carrying the Sun God’s blessing.","That was the person who should have encountered the Monarch of Decay. That was how the plan was supposed to proceed.","Yet something had gone wrong. Someone else had entered. A completely unexpected variable.","A young human who should never have been there.","\"This isn’t how it was supposed to happen...\"","The man’s voice became colder.","\"This isn’t what I expected.\"","The Monarch of Decay immediately noticed his reaction.","Its enormous mouth stretched into a grotesque. \"I don’t care what you are talking about!!\"","The man slowly looked upward again.","The creature continued speaking. \"That boy and the Moon Goddess damaged my soul.\"","Its voice was filled with rage.","\"Do you have any idea what that means?\"","Dark-red energy exploded from its body.","\"My soul has been damaged!\"","The surrounding space distorted violently.","\"And it’s all because of you!\"","The creature suddenly raised its enormous arm. Countless tentacles erupted from its flesh.","\"YOU WILL PAY FOR IT!\"","The arm descended.","BOOOOOOOOOOM!!!","A colossal wave of dark-red energy rushed toward the planet.","The attack was so enormous that it covered the entire mountain range.","The man’s expression didn’t change.","He simply bent his knees.","BOOM!","He kicked the ground. The mountain beneath his feet exploded. His body shot upward.","The attack passed beneath him. The sheer speed of his movement was beyond what ordinary perception could follow. His black hair whipped violently behind him as he ascended into space.","The Monarch of Decay’s gigantic eye followed him. Then the man’s body began changing. Black energy erupted from his skin.","RUMBLE.","His muscles expanded. His bones shifted. His entire body began growing at an impossible rate. He was changing into something huge. Something very dangerous."]}]);
